  ["deity.vecna.dmg2014"]={title="Vecna",subtitle="Divindade - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 10"},
  ["deity.vecna.egw2014"]={title="Vecna",subtitle="Divindade - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\nThe lich lord Vecna presides over villainous mages, conspiring politicians, and envious servants as the dark god of necromancy, undeath, and secrets. Once a dangerously clever and powerful archmage-turned-lich, his hunger for dominion over all mysteries and obsession with conquering the pantheon led to his own dissolution, leaving behind only his left hand and eye. His enduring spirit reformed through the ages and managed to reconstruct the Raven Queen's rites of ascension to become the newest of gods to walk Exandria. Defeated by the legendary heroes Vox Machina and sealed behind the Divine Gate, the Whispered One now quietly rules over that which is not meant to be known.\n\nVecna calls no place among the planes his home, instead wandering in search of powerful artifacts and secrets to further his unknowable plots.\n\nDepiction\n\nThose who claim to have looked on Vecna's form speak of a tall, skeletal lich swathed in tattered robes and enchanted jewels, missing both his left hand and left eye.\n\nEnemies\n\nWhile Vecna loathes all other gods and wishes to destroy them and become the sole divine power in the planes, he has a particular hatred for Ioun. Ioun seeks to share with the world the same secrets Vecna guards for himself, and his followers work diligently to undermine and destroy the Library of the Cobalt Soul and any others who follow her path. The Raven Queen also despises Vecna, and sees his presence as a mighty affront to her purpose.\n\nCommandments of Vecna\n\n• Learn all you can, and keep hidden that which you know. Reveal what pieces you must, but never the whole.\n\n• Express and cultivate the evil within yourself, and in doing so, recognize it in others to exploit them for your own benefit.\n\n• Seed the ruin of all who worship other deities, until only those who kneel before Vecna remain."},
  ["deity.vecna.phb2014"]={title="Vecna",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 295"},
  ["deity.vecna.xdmg2024"]={title="Vecna",subtitle="Divindade - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 148"},
  ["creature.vecna-impersonator.tofw2014"]={title="Vecna Impersonator",subtitle="Criatura - ToFW - 2014",body="Pagina: 26\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.vecna-the-archlich.vd2014"]={title="Vecna the Archlich",subtitle="Criatura - VD - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 26\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 272 (32d8 + 128)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 16 | CON 18 | INT 22 | WIS 24 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Elvish, Infernal\n\nResistencias: cold, lightning, necrotic\n\nImunidades: \n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned, stunned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (5/Day)\n\nIf Vecna fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nVecna carries a magic dagger named Afterthought. In the hands of anyone other than Vecna, Afterthought is a +2 dagger.\n\nUndying\n\nIf Vecna is slain, his soul refuses to accept its fate and lives on as a disembodied spirit that fashions a new body for itself after 1d100 years. Vecna's soul can fashion a new body even if its old body was burned to ash or otherwise obliterated. When the new body is complete, Vecna regains all his hit points and becomes active again. Vecna's new body appears anywhere within 100 miles of where Vecna was slain.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nVecna doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nVecna uses Flight of the Damned (if available), Rotten Fate, or Spellcasting. He then makes two attacks with Afterthought.\n\nAfterthought\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d4 + 5) piercing damage, plus 9 (2d8) necrotic damage. If the target is a creature, it is afflicted by entropic magic, taking 9 (2d8) necrotic damage at the start of each of its turns. Immediately after taking this damage on its turn, the target can make a 20 Constitution saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success. Until it succeeds on this save, the afflicted target can't regain hit points.\n\nFlight of the Damned {@recharge 5}\n\nVecna conjures a torrent of flying, spectral entities that fill a 120-foot cone and pass through all creatures in that area before dissipating. Each creature in that area must make a 22 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 36 (8d8) necrotic damage and is frightened of Vecna for 1 minute. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't frightened. A frightened creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nRotten Fate\n\nVecna causes necrotic magic to engulf one creature he can see within 120 feet of himself. The target must make a 22 Constitution saving throw, taking 96 (8d8 + 60) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A Humanoid killed by this magic rises as a zombie at the start of Vecna's next turn and acts immediately after Vecna in the initiative order. The zombie is under Vecna's control.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nVile Teleport\n\nVecna teleports, along with any equipment he is wearing or carrying, up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space he can see. He can cause each creature of his choice within 15 feet of his destination space to take 10 (3d6) psychic damage. If at least one creature takes this damage, Vecna regains 80 hit points.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nDread Counterspell\n\nVecna utters a dread word to interrupt a creature he can see that is casting a spell. If the spell is 4th level or lower, it fails and has no effect. If the spell is 5th level or higher, Vecna makes an Intelligence check (10 + the spell's level). On a success, the spell fails and has no effect. Whatever the spell's level, the caster takes 10 (3d6) psychic damage if the spell fails.\n\nFell Rebuke\n\nIn response to being hit by an attack, Vecna utters a fell word, dealing 10 (3d6) necrotic damage to the attacker, and Vecna teleports, along with any equipment he is wearing or carrying, up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space he can see."},
  ["creature.vecna-the-archlich.veor2014"]={title="Vecna the Archlich",subtitle="Criatura - VEoR - 2014",body="Pagina: 254\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 26\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 272 (32d8 + 128)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 16 | CON 18 | INT 22 | WIS 24 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Elvish, Infernal\n\nResistencias: cold, lightning, necrotic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned, stunned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (5/Day)\n\nIf Vecna fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nVecna carries a magic dagger named Afterthought. In the hands of anyone other than Vecna, Afterthought is a +2 Dagger.\n\nUndying\n\nIf Vecna is slain, his soul refuses to accept its fate and lives on as a disembodied spirit that fashions a new body for itself after 1d100 years. Vecna's new body appears within 100 miles of where he was slain. When the new body is complete, Vecna regains all his hit points and becomes active again.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nVecna uses Flight of the Damned (if available), Rotten Fate, or Spellcasting. He then makes two attacks with Afterthought.\n\nAfterthought\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d4 + 5) piercing damage plus 9 (2d8) necrotic damage. If the target is a creature, it is afflicted by entropic magic, taking 9 (2d8) necrotic damage at the start of each of its turns. Immediately after taking this damage on its turn, the target must make a 20 Constitution saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success. Until it succeeds on this save, the afflicted target can't regain hit points.\n\nFlight of the Damned {@recharge 5}\n\nVecna conjures a torrent of flying, spectral entities that fill a 120-foot cone and pass through all creatures in that area before dissipating. Each creature in that area must make a 22 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 36 (8d8) necrotic damage and has the frightened condition for 1 minute. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage only. A frightened creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nRotten Fate\n\nVecna causes necrotic magic to engulf one creature he can see within 120 feet of himself. The target must make a 22 Constitution saving throw, taking 96 (8d8 + 60) necrotic damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. A Humanoid killed by this magic rises as a zombie at the start of Vecna's next turn and acts immediately after Vecna in the initiative order. The zombie is under Vecna's control.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nVile Teleport\n\nVecna teleports, along with any equipment he is wearing or carrying, up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space he can see. He can cause each creature of his choice within 15 feet of his destination space to take 10 (3d6) psychic damage. If at least one creature takes this damage, Vecna regains 80 hit points.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nDread Counterspell\n\nVecna utters a dread word to interrupt a creature he can see that is casting a spell. If the spell is 4th level or lower, it fails and has no effect. If the spell is 5th level or higher, Vecna makes an Intelligence check (10 plus the spell's level). On a successful check, the spell fails and has no effect. Whatever the spell's level, the caster takes 10 (3d6) psychic damage if the spell fails.\n\nFell Rebuke\n\nIn response to being hit by an attack, Vecna utters a fell word, dealing 10 (3d6) necrotic damage to the attacker, and Vecna teleports, along with any equipment he is wearing or carrying, up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space he can see."},
  ["language.vedalken.ggr2014"]={title="Vedalken",subtitle="Idioma - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\nThe Vedalken language is renowned for its technical treatises and its catalogs of knowledge about the natural world and the aether that pervades it."},
  ["species.vedalken.ggr2014"]={title="Vedalken",subtitle="Especie - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nAge\n\nVedalken mature slower than humans do, reaching maturity around age 40. Their life span is typically 350 years, with some living to the age of 500.\n\nAlignment\n\nVedalken are usually lawful and non-evil.\n\nSize\n\nTall and slender, Vedalken stand 6 to 6½ feet tall on average and usually weigh less than 200 pounds. Your size is Medium.\n\nVedalken Dispassion\n\nYou have advantage on all Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma saving throws.\n\nTireless Precision\n\nYou are proficient in one of the following skills of your choice: Arcana, History, Investigation, Medicine, Performance, or Sleight of Hand. You are also proficient with one phb of your choice.\n\nWhenever you make an ability check with the chosen skill or tool, roll a d4 and add the number rolled to the check's total.\n\nPartially Amphibious\n\nBy absorbing oxygen through your skin, you can breathe underwater for up to 1 hour. Once you've reached that limit, you can't use this trait again until you finish a long rest.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common, Vedalken, and one other language of your choice."},
  ["species.vedalken.psk2014"]={title="Vedalken",subtitle="Especie - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 23\n\nAge\n\nVedalken mature at the same rate humans do, and most are expected to settle down into an adult life by around age 40. They can live 350 to almost 500 years.\n\nAlignment\n\nVedalken are most often lawful and rarely evil.\n\nSize\n\nVedalken are taller than humans but more slender. They average 6 to 6½ feet tall, but usually weigh less than 200 pounds. Your size is Medium.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and Vedalken. The Vedalken language is renowned for its technical treatises and its catalogs of knowledge about the natural world and the aether that pervades it.\n\nVedalken Cunning\n\nYou have advantage on all Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma saving throws against magic.\n\nAether Lore\n\nWhenever you make an Intelligence (History) check related to magic items or aether-powered technological devices, you can add twice your proficiency bonus, instead of any proficiency bonus you normally apply."},
  ["creature.vegepygmy.mpmm2014"]={title="Vegepygmy",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 252\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 13 (3d6 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 7 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 6 | WIS 11 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Vegepygmy\n\nResistencias: lightning, piercing\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPlant Camouflage\n\nThe vegepygmy has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks it makes in any terrain with ample obscuring vegetation.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe vegepygmy regains 3 hit points at the start of its turn. If it takes cold, fire, or necrotic damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of the vegepygmy's next turn. The vegepygmy dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaws\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nSling\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.vegepygmy.vgm2014"]={title="Vegepygmy",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 196\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 9 (2d6 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 7 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 6 | WIS 11 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Vegepygmy\n\nResistencias: lightning, piercing\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPlant Camouflage\n\nThe vegepygmy has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks it makes in any terrain with ample obscuring plant life.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe vegepygmy regains 3 hit points at the start of its turn. If it takes cold, fire, or necrotic damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of the vegepygmy's next turn. The vegepygmy dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaws\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nSling\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["language.vegepygmy.vgm2014"]={title="Vegepygmy",subtitle="Idioma - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 196"},
  ["creature.vegepygmy-chief.mpmm2014"]={title="Vegepygmy Chief",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 253\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / S\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 33 (6d6 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 7 | WIS 12 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Vegepygmy\n\nResistencias: lightning, piercing\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPlant Camouflage\n\nThe vegepygmy has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks it makes in any terrain with ample obscuring vegetation.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe vegepygmy regains 5 hit points at the start of its turn. If it takes cold, fire, or necrotic damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of the vegepygmy's next turn. The vegepygmy dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe vegepygmy makes two Claw attacks or two melee Spear attacks.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack.\n\nSpores (1/Day)\n\nA 15-foot-radius cloud of toxic spores extends out from the vegepygmy. The spores spread around corners. Each creature in that area that isn't a Plant must succeed on a 12 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned. While poisoned in this way, a target takes 9 (2d8) poison damage at the start of each of its turns. A target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.vegepygmy-chief.vgm2014"]={title="Vegepygmy Chief",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 197\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / S\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 33 (6d6 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 7 | WIS 12 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Vegepygmy\n\nResistencias: lightning, piercing\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPlant Camouflage\n\nThe vegepygmy has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks it makes in any terrain with ample obscuring plant life.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe vegepygmy regains 5 hit points at the start of its turn. If it takes cold, fire, or necrotic damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of the vegepygmy's next turn. The vegepygmy dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe vegepygmy makes two attacks with its claws or two melee attacks with its spear.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack.\n\nSpores (1/Day)\n\nA 15-foot-radius cloud of toxic spores extends out from the vegepygmy. The spores spread around corners. Each creature in that area that isn't a plant must succeed on a 12 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned. While poisoned in this way, a target takes 9 (2d8) poison damage at the start of each of its turns. A target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.vegepygmy-moldmaker.qftis2014"]={title="Vegepygmy Moldmaker",subtitle="Criatura - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 218\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / S\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 44 (8d6 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 16 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Vegepygmy\n\nResistencias: lightning, piercing\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPlant Camouflage\n\nThe vegepygmy has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks it makes in any terrain with ample obscuring vegetation.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe vegepygmy regains 7 hit points at the start of its turn. If it takes cold, fire, or necrotic damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of the vegepygmy's next turn. The vegepygmy dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe vegepygmy makes two Claw attacks.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (3d6 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nToxic Mold (2/Day)\n\nThe vegepygmy targets a creature it can see within 60 feet of itself. If the target isn't a vegepygmy, it must make a 13 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the target takes 13 (3d8) poison damage and has the blinded and deafened conditions for 1 minute as it becomes covered in a thick layer of mold. On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage only.\n\nThe target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.vegepygmy-scavenger.qftis2014"]={title="Vegepygmy Scavenger",subtitle="Criatura - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 218\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 13 (3d6 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 7 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 6 | WIS 11 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Vegepygmy\n\nResistencias: lightning, piercing\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPlant Camouflage\n\nThe vegepygmy has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks it makes in any terrain with ample obscuring vegetation.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe vegepygmy regains 3 hit points at the start of its turn. If it takes cold, fire, or necrotic damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of the vegepygmy's next turn. The vegepygmy dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaw\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nSling\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) bludgeoning damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nNimble Escape\n\nThe vegepygmy takes the Disengage or Hide action."},
  ["creature.vegepygmy-thorny-hunter.qftis2014"]={title="Vegepygmy Thorny Hunter",subtitle="Criatura - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 219\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 27 (5d8 + 5)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: lightning, piercing\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe vegepygmy has advantage on attack rolls against a creature if at least one of the vegepygmy's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally doesn't have the incapacitated condition.\n\nPlant Camouflage\n\nThe vegepygmy has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks it makes in any terrain with ample obscuring vegetation.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe vegepygmy regains 5 hit points at the start of its turn. If it takes cold, fire, or necrotic damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of the vegepygmy's next turn. The vegepygmy dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\nThorny Body\n\nAt the start of its turn, the vegepygmy deals 2 (1d4) piercing damage to any creature grappling it.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d8 + 2) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 12 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition."},
  ["creature.veiled-presence.bmt2014"]={title="Veiled Presence",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 48\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / S/M\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 300 (40d8 + 120)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 24 | CON 16 | INT 24 | WIS 20 | CHA 22\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all\n\nResistencias: necrotic, radiant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nInviolate Presence\n\nThe veiled presence can't be targeted by divination magic or by features that would read its mind or determine its creature type.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the veiled presence fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe veiled presence makes two Blade of Judgment attacks and can use Revelation.\n\nBlade of Judgment\n\nmw,rw 14 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft., one target. h10 (1d6 + 7) piercing damage plus 27 (6d8) radiant damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 22 Charisma saving throw, or on its next turn, it can either move or take an action, but not both.\n\nRevelation\n\nThe veiled presence reveals a glimpse of its otherworldly nature to a creature it can see within 30 feet of itself. The target must succeed on a 22 Wisdom saving throw or have the paralyzed condition until the end of its next turn, after which the target is immune to this Revelation for 24 hours.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nUncanny Dodge\n\nWhen an attacker the veiled presence can see hits the veiled presence with an attack, the veiled presence halves the attack's damage against it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nFlash Step\n\nThe veiled presence magically teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 40 feet to an unoccupied space that it can see.\n\nStab (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe veiled presence makes one Blade of Judgment attack.\n\nSearing Radiance (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe veiled presence magically emanates dazzling light in a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on itself until the end of its next turn, during which time attack rolls against it have disadvantage and it has advantage on attack rolls. The sphere moves with the veiled presence. When another creature starts its turn in the light or enters the light for the first time on its turn, that creature must make a 22 Constitution saving throw, taking 18 (4d8) radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.veldyskar.oota2014"]={title="Veldyskar",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nINT 10\n\nIdiomas: Common, Dwarvish, Giant, Undercommon\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting"},
  ["creature.vellin-farstride.mabjov2014"]={title="Vellin Farstride",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 62\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 195 (30d6 + 90)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 20 | CON 16 | INT 11 | WIS 14 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Halfling, Infernal, telepathy 30 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAnimal Companions\n\nVellin is accompanied by Akela (wolf with 18 hit points). Vellin can mount or dismount Akela using 5 feet of movement. While mounted, Vellin can order Akela to Dash, Disengage, and Dodge. In addition, Vellin has an owl companion with 3 hit points. On Vellin's turn, the owl can perform a flyby on a creature of Vellin's choice. The next attack that Vellin makes against that creature has advantage.\n\nBrave\n\nVellin has advantage on saving throws against being frightened.\n\nFiend Slayer\n\nWhen Vellin hits a Fiend with a weapon attack he deals an additional 7 (2d6) radiant damage.\n\nKeen Hearing and Sight\n\nVellin has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or sight.\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nVellin wields a +1 shortsword (silvered) and a +1 shield.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nVellin makes three Silvered Shortsword attacks.\n\nSilvered Shortsword\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d6 + 6) piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nNimble Escape\n\nVellin can take the Disengage or Hide action."},
  ["creature.vellynne-harpell.idrotf2014"]={title="Vellynne Harpell",subtitle="Criatura - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 273\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 67 (9d8 + 27)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 12 | CON 17 | INT 18 | WIS 15 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Dwarvish, Elvish, Orc\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nVellynne wears bracers of defense and carries a wand of magic missiles (see \"Actions\" below).\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nVampiric Touch (3rd-Level Spell; Requires a Spell Slot)\n\nms 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h10 (3d6) necrotic damage, and Vellynne regains hit points equal to half the necrotic damage dealt. If Vellynne casts this spell using a spell slot of 4th level or higher, the necrotic damage increases by 1d6 for each slot level above 3rd.\n\nChill Touch (Cantrip)\n\nrs 6 to hit, range 120 ft., one creature. h9 (2d8) necrotic damage, and the target can't regain hit points until the start of Vellynne's next turn.\n\nWand of Magic Missiles\n\nWhile holding this wand, Vellynne can expend 1 or more of its 7 charges to cast the magic missile spell from it. She can expend 1 charge to cast the 1st-level version of the spell. She can increase the spell slot level by one for each additional charge she expends. The wand regains 1d6 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn. If the wand's last charge is expended, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed."},
  ["creature.velociraptor.mpmm2014"]={title="Velociraptor",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 96\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / T\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 10 (3d4 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 4 | WIS 12 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe velociraptor has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the velociraptor's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe velociraptor makes one Bite attack and one Claw attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.velociraptor.vgm2014"]={title="Velociraptor",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 140\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / T\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 10 (3d4 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 4 | WIS 12 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe velociraptor has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the velociraptor's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe velociraptor makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.velomachus-lorehold.scc2014"]={title="Velomachus Lorehold",subtitle="Criatura - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 219\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 25\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 487 (25d20 + 225)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 14 | CON 29 | INT 30 | WIS 20 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all\n\nImunidades: thunder\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Velomachus fails a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nVelomachus makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h15 (1d10 + 10) piercing damage plus 6 (1d12) thunder damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h13 (1d6 + 10) slashing damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it is knocked prone.\n\nBattle Tide Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nVelomachus exhales thunderous sound in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 25 Constitution saving throw. On a failure, a creature takes 45 (7d12) force damage and 45 (7d12) thunder damage and is pushed up to 20 feet in a horizontal direction of Velomachus' choice. On a success, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't pushed. Objects that aren't being worn or carried take the damage and are pushed as if they were creatures that failed the saving throw.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nVelomachus makes one Claw attack.\n\nChaotic Flow (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nVelomachus moves up to half her flying speed. If a creature hits or misses her with an opportunity attack during this move, the attacker takes 19 (3d12) thunder damage.\n\nRepeating History (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nVelomachus magically summons 1d4 SCC in unoccupied spaces she can see within 60 feet of herself. The spirit statues obey her commands and take their turns immediately after hers. Any creature, other than a spirit statue or Velomachus, is restrained if it starts its turn within 5 feet of one or more of these spirit statues. This restrained condition lasts until the end of the creature's turn. These spirit statues disappear after 10 minutes, when Velomachus dies, or when she uses this action again."},
  ["item.velvet-doublet-with-gold-buttons-legion-of-dusk.psx2014"]={title="Velvet doublet with gold buttons (Legion of Dusk)",subtitle="Item - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["vehicle.venatrix.veor2014"]={title="Venatrix",subtitle="Veiculo - VEoR - 2014",body="Pagina: 151"},
  ["feature.vengeful-ancestors.xge2024.barbarian.ancestral-guardian.14"]={title="Vengeful Ancestors",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 9\n\nAt 14th level, your ancestral spirits grow powerful enough to retaliate. When you use your Spirit Shield to reduce the damage of an attack, the attacker takes an amount of force damage equal to the damage that your Spirit Shield prevents."},
  ["creature.venger.au2014"]={title="Venger",subtitle="Criatura - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 202 (27d8 + 81)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 20 | CON 16 | INT 17 | WIS 14 | CHA 21\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft. (unimpeded by magical {@variantrule Darkness|XPHB})\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Infernal\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFiendish Restoration\n\nIf Venger dies, his body dissipates into crimson dust, and he gains a new body in 1d10 days, reviving with all his XPHB somewhere in one of his lairs.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Lair)\n\nIf Venger fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nVenger has XPHB on saving throws against spells and magical effects.\n\nMounted Adept\n\nWhile Venger is mounted, he and his mount have XPHB on Dexterity saving throws, and Venger can force an attack targeting his mount to target him instead. Venger can't use this trait if he has the XPHB condition.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nTelekinesis (2/Day)\n\nProtective Magic\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nVenger makes three attacks, using Crimson Claw or Crimson Blast in any combination.\n\nCrimson Claw\n\nm 11, reach 5 ft. h14 (2d8 + 5) Slashing damage plus 10 (3d6) Fire damage.\n\nCrimson Blast\n\nr 11, range 120 ft. h24 (3d12 + 5) Force damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nBooming Censure\n\nwis 19, one creature Venger can see within 60 feet. actSaveFail 14 (4d6) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\nCrimson Strike\n\nVenger makes one Crimson Claw or Crimson Blast attack.\n\nMagic-Binding Chains\n\ndex 19, one creature Venger can see within 30 feet. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. While XPHB, the target can't take the XPHB action. actSaveSuccessOrFail Venger can't take this action again until the start of his next turn."},
  ["creature.venom-troll.mpmm2014"]={title="Venom Troll",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 248\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 94 (9d10 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 13 | CON 20 | INT 7 | WIS 9 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Giant\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPoison Splash\n\nWhen the troll takes damage of any type but psychic, each creature within 5 feet of the troll takes 9 (2d8) poison damage.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe troll regains 10 hit points at the start of each of its turns. If the troll takes acid or fire damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of the troll's next turn. The troll dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe troll makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) poison damage, and the creature is poisoned until the start of the troll's next turn.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) poison damage.\n\nVenom Spray {@recharge}\n\nThe troll slices itself with a claw, releasing a spray of poison in a 15-foot cube. The troll takes 7 (2d6) slashing damage (this damage can't be reduced in any way). Each creature in the area must make a 16 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 18 (4d8) poison damage and is poisoned for 1 minute. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't poisoned. A poisoned creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.venom-troll.mtf2014"]={title="Venom Troll",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 245\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 94 (9d10 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 13 | CON 20 | INT 7 | WIS 9 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Giant\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Smell\n\nThe troll has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.\n\nPoison Splash\n\nWhen the troll takes damage of any type but psychic, each creature within 5 feet of the troll takes 9 (2d8) poison damage.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe troll regains 10 hit points at the start of each of its turns. If the troll takes acid or fire damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of the troll's next turn. The troll dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe troll makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) poison damage, and the creature is poisoned until the start of the troll's next turn.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) poison damage.\n\nVenom Spray {@recharge}\n\nThe troll slices itself with a claw, releasing a spray of poison in a 15-foot cube. The troll takes 7 (2d6) slashing damage (this damage can't be reduced in any way). Each creature in the area must make a 16 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 18 (4d8) poison damage and is poisoned for 1 minute. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't poisoned. A poisoned creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.venomfang.lmop2014"]={title="Venomfang",subtitle="Criatura - LMoP - 2014",body="Pagina: 63\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.venomous-snake.xmm2024"]={title="Venomous Snake",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 372\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / T\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 5 (2d4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 2 | DEX 15 | CON 11 | INT 1 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nSentidos: Blindsight 10 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) Poison damage."},
  ["magicitem.ventilating-lungs.erlw2014"]={title="Ventilating Lungs",subtitle="Item Magico - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 279\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThese metallic nodules were created in response to the poisonous gases used on the battlefields of the Last War. When you attune to these lungs, they replace the lungs in your chest, which disappear. The lungs allow you to breathe normally, even in an antimagic field, and their breathing function can't be suppressed by magic.\n\nOutside an antimagic field or any other effect that suppresses magic, these lungs allow you to breathe normally in any environment (including a vacuum), and you have advantage on saving throws against harmful gases such as those created by a cloudkill spell, a stinking cloud spell, inhaled poisons, and gaseous breath weapons.\n\nAs an action, you can use these lungs to exhale a gust of wind, as if you had cast the gust of wind spell (spell save 15) with no components. This property of the lungs can't be used again until the next dawn.\n\nIf your attunement to the lungs ends, your original lungs reappear."},
  ["creature.verbeeg-longstrider.idrotf2014"]={title="Verbeeg Longstrider",subtitle="Criatura - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 311\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 119 (14d10 + 42)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 15 | CON 16 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSimple Weapon Wielder\n\nA simple weapon deals one extra die of its damage when the verbeeg hits with it (included in the attack).\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe verbeeg makes two melee attacks.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h14 (3d6 + 4) piercing damage, or 17 (3d8 + 4) piercing damage if used to make a ranged attack or used with two hands to make a melee attack.\n\nSling\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h9 (3d4 + 2) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or be stunned until the end of its next turn."},
  ["creature.verbeeg-marauder.idrotf2014"]={title="Verbeeg Marauder",subtitle="Criatura - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 311\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / L\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 85 (10d10 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 11 | CON 16 | INT 11 | WIS 10 | CHA 9\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSimple Weapon Wielder\n\nA simple weapon deals one extra die of its damage when the verbeeg hits with it (included in the attack).\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe verbeeg makes two melee attacks.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h14 (3d6 + 4) piercing damage, or 17 (3d8 + 4) piercing damage if used to make a ranged attack or used with two hands to make a melee attack."},
  ["species.verdan.ai2014"]={title="Verdan",subtitle="Especie - AI - 2014",body="Pagina: 72\n\nAge\n\nVerdan reach adulthood at around the age of 24, and it is thought that they might live to nearly 200 years old. However, because no verdan has died of old age since the race's initial creation, their upper age limits remain subject to speculation.\n\nAlignment\n\nVerdan are generally good, although their absence of racial identity and shared history can sometimes see individual verdan become untethered from any moral or ethical framework.\n\nSize\n\nVerdan start out similar in size to the goblins they were created from, ranging from 3 to 4 feet in height. But at some point after reaching maturity, each verdan undergoes a sudden growth spurt of 2 feet or more. At 1st level, you are a Small creature. When you reach 5th level, you become a Medium creature.\n\nBlack Blood Healing\n\nThe black blood that is a sign of your people's connection to That-Which-Endures boosts your natural healing. When you roll a 1 or 2 on any Hit Die you spend at the end of a short rest, you can reroll the die and must use the new roll.\n\nLimited Telepathy\n\nYou can telepathically speak to any creature you can see within 30 feet of you. You don't need to share a language with the creature for it to understand your telepathy, but it must be able to understand at least one language. This process of communication is slow and limited, allowing you to transmit and receive only simple ideas and straightforward concepts.\n\nPersuasive\n\nYour people's lack of history makes you trustworthy and humble. You have proficiency in the Persuasion skill.\n\nTelepathic Insight\n\nYour mind's connection to the world around you strengthens your will. You have advantage on all Wisdom and Charisma saving throws.\n\nLanguage\n\nYou speak, read, and write Common, Goblin, and one additional language of your choice. This language typically has some connection to one of the areas or cultures that has been part of your life."},
  ["deity.vergadain.mtf2014"]={title="Vergadain",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 73"},
  ["deity.vergadain.scag2014"]={title="Vergadain",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 22"},
  ["creature.verin-thelyss.crcotn2014"]={title="Verin Thelyss",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 51\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 84 (13d8 + 26)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 15 | CON 14 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish, Undercommon\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nVerin has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put him to sleep.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, Verin has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nVerin makes three Glaive attacks.\n\nGlaive\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h9 (1d10 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nHand Crossbow\n\nrw 7 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage plus 22 (4d10) poison damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nManifest Echo\n\nVerin magically creates an echo—a translucent, gray object that looks like him. The echo appears in an unoccupied space Verin can see within 15 feet of himself. While the echo exists, Verin chooses whether each of his attacks originates from his space or the echo's space. On Verin's turn, the echo can move in accordance with Verin's wishes. The echo has AC 17 and 1 hit point. It otherwise uses Verin's statistics. The echo lasts for 1 minute or until it is destroyed, until Verin ends his turn more than 30 feet away from it, until Verin manifests another echo, or until Verin is incapacitated.\n\nReposition\n\nVerin magically swaps places with his echo.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nVerin adds 3 to his AC against one melee attack that would hit him. To do so, he must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon."},
  ["creature.verminaard.mcv2dc2014"]={title="Verminaard",subtitle="Criatura - MCV2DC - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 143 (22d8 + 44)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 13 | CON 15 | INT 16 | WIS 18 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDraconic Command\n\nWhenever a Dragon or a creature with the Draconic Devotion trait within 30 feet of Verminaard makes an attack roll, the creature can roll a d4 and add the number rolled to the attack roll.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Verminaard fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nVerminaard wears +2 plate armor and wields the mace MCV2DC, which grants him darkvision as well as immunity to fire damage and to the charmed and frightened conditions (included above).\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nVerminaard makes two Nightbringer attacks and uses Malediction.\n\nNightbringer\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (1d6 + 9) bludgeoning damage plus 10 (4d4) radiant damage. If the target is a creature, the target must succeed on a 20 Constitution saving throw or be blinded until the start of Verminaard's next turn.\n\nMalediction\n\nVerminaard utters an unholy word, causing profane fire to descend on one creature Verminaard can see within 60 feet of himself. The creature must make a 18 Dexterity saving throw, taking 11 (2d10) necrotic damage plus 11 (2d10) radiant damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nDragon Queen's Favor (5/Day)\n\nVerminaard or one creature he can see within 60 feet of himself magically regains 17 (2d12 + 4) hit points.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nTactical Movement\n\nVerminaard moves up to his speed or commands a mount he is riding to move up to its speed. This movement doesn't provoke opportunity attacks.\n\nFervent Strike (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nVerminaard makes one Nightbringer attack. If this attack hits, it deals an additional 7 (2d6) bludgeoning damage.\n\nCast a Spell (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nVerminaard uses Spellcasting."},
  ["item.verminshroud-awakened.egw2014"]={title="Verminshroud (Awakened)",subtitle="Item - EGW - 2014",body=""},
  ["magicitem.verminshroud-dormant.egw2014"]={title="Verminshroud (Dormant)",subtitle="Item Magico - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 273\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis patchy cloak was pieced together from the pelts of rats found feasting on the dead in Blightshore and is dotted with the bloated corpses of magically preserved insects along its seams.\n\nDormant\n\nWhile wearing the Verminshroud in its dormant state, you gain the following benefits:\n\n• You have advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell, you are immune to disease, and you have darkvision out to a range of 60 feet. If you already have darkvision, wearing the cloak increases the range of your darkvision by 60 feet.\n\n• As an action, you can use the Verminshroud to cast polymorph on yourself, transforming into a giant rat or rat while retaining your Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores, as well as the properties of the cloak. This property can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["item.verminshroud-exalted.egw2014"]={title="Verminshroud (Exalted)",subtitle="Item - EGW - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.versatile-trickster.phb2014.rogue.arcane-trickster.13"]={title="Versatile Trickster",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 97\n\nAt 13th level, you gain the ability to distract targets with your mage hand. As a bonus action on your turn, you can designate a creature within 5 feet of the spectral hand created by the spell. Doing so gives you advantage on attack rolls against that creature until the end of the turn."},
  ["feature.versatile-trickster.xphb2024.rogue.arcane-trickster.13"]={title="Versatile Trickster",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 133\n\nYou gain the ability to distract targets with your XPHB. When you use the Trip option of your Cunning Strike on a creature, you can also use that option on another creature within 5 feet of the spectral hand."},
  ["creature.vertrand-shadowdusk.wdmm2014"]={title="Vertrand Shadowdusk",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 282\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Deep Speech, Undercommon"},
  ["deity.vesh.egw2014"]={title="Vesh",subtitle="Divindade - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\nNone know whether Vesh is a witch or a demigod, but she has walked Exandria for centuries, seducing those who pry into forbidden magics and drawing them to her as possible suitors. Acolytes cultivate sects of worshipers who engage in ritualistic orgies and masochistic rites, these hedonistic rituals culminating with her selection of a mate. Vesh feeds on the unchosen in a bloody massacre before laying with her selected survivor and vanishing to her realm. Their essences intertwined, she then lends her strength to her mate, watching over them for life.\n\nA being with conflicting duality, Vesh has moods that demand sacrifice and pain, and others that ask for benevolence and mercy. Because Vesh's whims are truly unknown, many who wish to gain her favor and attention commit terrible acts. While she has many partners, she is a jealous patron who demands the true heart of her chosen. Those who stray are never heard from again.\n\nAppearance\n\nVesh resembles a nude woman with faintly glowing gray skin, long purple hair, and unnaturally long arms and fingers that end in claw-like nails. Her eyes are pale white with no iris, and her expression varies from alluring to monstrous depending on her mood."},
  ["feature.vestige-companion.au2014.warlock.vestige.3"]={title="Vestige Companion",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.vestige-companion.au2014"]={title="Vestige Companion",subtitle="Criatura - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 14\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: {'choose': ['celestial', 'fiend', 'undead']} / S\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, fly: 30\n\nSTR 1 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 15 | WIS 15 | CHA 16\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: speaks the languages you know\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPact Bond\n\nAdd your XPHB to any ability check or saving throw the vestige makes.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nVestige's Strike\n\nm,r Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft. h1d6 + 3 plus your Charisma modifier Fire (Fiend), Necrotic (Undead), or Radiant (Celestial) damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nDivine Power (1/Day)\n\nYour vestige manifests a remnant of its divine power in one of the following ways, based on its form:\n\nCursed Invocation (Undead Only)\n\nThe vestige places a curse on a creature you can see within 30 feet of the vestige for 1 minute. While cursed, the target has XPHB on attack rolls against you and the vestige.\n\nFiendish Swap (Fiend Only)\n\nIf you and the vestige are within 60 feet of each other, you both teleport, swapping places.\n\nHealing Touch (Celestial Only)\n\nThe vestige touches another creature. The target regains XPHB equal to 2d8 plus your Charisma modifier and ends one condition on it: XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB."},
  ["subclass.vestige-patron.au2014.warlock.vestige.0"]={title="Vestige Patron",subtitle="Subclasse - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 13\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Vestige Companion\n\nPagina: 13\n\nThe vestige manifests, drawing strength from your pact. It uses the AU stat block and is a Celestial, Fiend, or Undead (choose when you gain this feature). You determine what the vestige looks like, but regardless of its form, the vestige bears features indicating its supernatural origin. For example, you might decide your vestige is an oversize floating skull etched with sigils, a circle of glowing runes, or a constantly shifting abstract shape. The vestige is XPHB to you and your allies and obeys your commands. It vanishes if you die.\n\nThe Vestige in Combat\n\nIn combat, the vestige acts during your turn. It can move and use its XPHB on its own, but the only action it takes is the XPHB action unless you take a XPHB to command it to take an action in its stat block or some other action. You can also sacrifice one of your attacks when you take the XPHB action to command the vestige to take the Vestige's Strike action. If you have the XPHB condition, the vestige acts on its own and isn't limited to the XPHB action.\n\nDisappearance of the Vestige\n\nWhen the vestige drops to 0 XPHB, it disappears. You can spend 1 minute performing a magical ceremony to manifest the vestige again; it reappears with its maximum XPHB in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you. As a XPHB action, you can temporarily dismiss the vestige to a pocket dimension. As a XPHB action while it is temporarily dismissed, you can cause the vestige to reappear in an unoccupied space within 30 feet of you. Whenever the vestige drops to 0 XPHB or disappears into the pocket dimension, it leaves behind in its space anything it was wearing or carrying.\n\nVestige Companion\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB, you can summon the vestige in a new form, which appears in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you. You choose its appearance and whether it is a Celestial, Fiend, or Undead. If the vestige is already manifested from this feature, its form changes to the new one.\n\nNivel 3 - Vestige Companion\n\nNivel 3 - Vestige Patron\n\nPagina: 13\n\nWield the Remnants of a Dying God's Power\n\nYour pact draws on the power of a dying god, a being once worshipped by countless followers but now abandoned and forgotten. This dying god, known as a vestige, might have been benevolent, evil, or strange and unknowable, but now it is driven to regain its former power. The vestige needs your help, and it is willing to share its remaining strength with you.\n\nNivel 3 - Vestige Spells\n\nPagina: 14\n\nThe magic of your AU ensures you always have certain spells ready. Select one of the following Cleric domains: XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB. The Domain Spells of your chosen domain are Warlock spells for you. When you reach a Warlock level equal to a Cleric level listed on the Domain Spells table for the domain you have chosen, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nFor example, if you chose the XPHB for this feature, when you reach Warlock level 3, you would have the XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB spells prepared.\n\nNivel 6 - Vestige Power\n\nPagina: 14\n\nYour AU now regains its use of Divine Power whenever you finish a XPHB or XPHB or when you use your Magical Cunning feature. In addition, while within 30 feet of your AU, you have XPHB to the same damage types as the vestige.\n\nNivel 6 - Vestige Power\n\nNivel 10 - Vestige Recovery\n\nPagina: 14\n\nWhen your AU would drop to 0 XPHB, you can take a XPHB and expend a Pact Magic spell slot to instead change its XPHB to its XPHB maximum. The vestige then teleports to an unoccupied space you can see within 30 feet of it. Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 10 - Vestige Recovery\n\nNivel 14 - Semblance of Life\n\nPagina: 14\n\nYour AU continues to grow in strength, and with your assistance, it can briefly adopt a more powerful form. Depending on the vestige's type, you can take a XPHB action while the vestige is within 90 feet of you to shape-shift it for 1 hour into one of the following forms: Celestial Spirit (Celestial vestige; see the XPHB spell in the XPHB), Fiendish Spirit (Fiend vestige; see the XPHB spell in the XPHB), or Undead Spirit (Undead vestige; see the XPHB spell in the XPHB). The vestige's game statistics are replaced by the spirit's stat block, and the spell's level is equal to half your Warlock level (round down; maximum level 9), but the vestige retains its personality, Divine Power XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB.\n\nThe vestige gains a number of XPHB equal to the XPHB of the spirit form. These XPHB vanish if any remain after 1 hour, and the transformation ends early if it has no XPHB left.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 14 - Semblance of Life"},
  ["feature.vestige-patron.au2014.warlock.vestige.3"]={title="Vestige Patron",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 13\n\nWield the Remnants of a Dying God's Power\n\nYour pact draws on the power of a dying god, a being once worshipped by countless followers but now abandoned and forgotten. This dying god, known as a vestige, might have been benevolent, evil, or strange and unknowable, but now it is driven to regain its former power. The vestige needs your help, and it is willing to share its remaining strength with you."},
  ["feature.vestige-power.au2014.warlock.vestige.6"]={title="Vestige Power",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.vestige-recovery.au2014.warlock.vestige.10"]={title="Vestige Recovery",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.vestige-spells.au2014.warlock.vestige.3"]={title="Vestige Spells",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 14\n\nThe magic of your AU ensures you always have certain spells ready. Select one of the following Cleric domains: XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB. The Domain Spells of your chosen domain are Warlock spells for you. When you reach a Warlock level equal to a Cleric level listed on the Domain Spells table for the domain you have chosen, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nFor example, if you chose the XPHB for this feature, when you reach Warlock level 3, you would have the XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB spells prepared."},
  ["creature.veteran.mm2014"]={title="Veteran",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 350\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 58 (9d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 13 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 11 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe veteran makes two longsword attacks. If it has a shortsword drawn, it can also make a shortsword attack.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) slashing damage, or 8 (1d10 + 3) slashing damage if used with two hands.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nHeavy Crossbow\n\nrw 3 to hit, range 100/400 ft., one target. h6 (1d10 + 1) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.veteran-of-the-gauntlet.oota2014"]={title="Veteran of the Gauntlet",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 130\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 58 (9d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 13 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 11 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Dwarvish\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe veteran makes two longsword attacks. If it has a shortsword drawn, it can also make a shortsword attack.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) slashing damage, or 8 (1d10 + 3) slashing damage if used with two hands.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nHeavy Crossbow\n\nrw 3 to hit, range 100/400 ft., one target. h6 (1d10 + 1) piercing damage."},
  ["magicitem.veteran-s-cane.xdmg2024"]={title="Veteran's Cane",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 318\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nAs a XPHB, you can transform this walking cane into an ordinary Longsword or change the Longsword back into a walking cane. In either case, you must be holding the item."},
  ["magicitem.veteran-s-cane.xge2024"]={title="Veteran's Cane",subtitle="Item Magico - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 139\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nWhen you grasp this walking cane and use a bonus action to speak the command word, it transforms into an ordinary longsword and ceases to be magical."},
  ["deity.vhaeraun.mtf2014"]={title="Vhaeraun",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 55\n\nVhaeraun stands for the dark elves' superiority over other races and for the primacy of individual drow over other drow. He is a god of arrogance, and thus he condones all acts of avarice, fair and foul alike. Those who take what they want from whom they wish, whether through stealth or bullying, pay homage to Vhaeraun. He is patron to thieves and often the object of prayer before drow embark on a raid.\n\nAmong the male gods of the Dark Seldarine, he is as widely recognized and accepted as Keptolo. But Vhaeraun represents a different aspect of drow masculinity: strong, silent, obedient, swift, and deadly. He is thought of as Lolth's favored son, in contrast to Keptolo's role as her beautiful consort.\n\nDue to his high status in the Dark Seldarine (for a male) and because of his arrogance, a few of his worshipers look on him as an advocate of equality between male and female drow. That heresy, when it is expressed openly, is liable to be savagely crushed by the priestesses of Lolth. So most of Vhaeraun's male followers honor him simply by trying to carve out better lives for themselves, and that activity is tolerated. Even so, adherents of Vhaeraun don't appear in public without wearing masks. This practice exists in part because Vhaeraun is never portrayed unmasked, and partly because anonymity is a wise precaution when one challenges the social structure of the drow in even a small way.\n\nTo quash any challenge to the matriarchy that Vhaeraun might inspire in his followers, some drow communities preach that he wears a mask to hide the terrible scars from the wounds inflicted on him by Lolth as punishment for his arrogance. His silence, too, is part of his punishment, for his tongue was removed for questioning Lolth's orders. Worshipers of Vhaeraun who believe this dogma sometimes ritually scar and silence themselves as signs of their devotion, and then serve as voiceless, masked bodyguards for the matrons of their house."},
  ["deity.vhaeraun.scag2014"]={title="Vhaeraun",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 23"},
  ["creature.vi-aroon.jttrc2014"]={title="Vi Aroon",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["item.vial.phb2014"]={title="Vial",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 153\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA vial can hold up to 4 ounces of liquid."},
  ["item.vial.xphb2024"]={title="Vial",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 229\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA Vial holds up to 4 ounces."},
  ["magicitem.vial-of-greed.coa2014"]={title="Vial of Greed",subtitle="Item Magico - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 270\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis small glass vial can stockpile resources for use in the future. Once stored, resources last for 1 century before vanishing. As an action you make the vial store any number of the following resources, which are magically consumed and converted into a violet-colored liquid:\n\n• Up to 31 days of food and/or drink. The flavors are lost, instead becoming tasteless.\n\n• Up to 7 days of alcohol. The flavors are lost, instead becoming tasteless.\n\n• Up to 5 magic scrolls that affect a single creature. The target of the spell is you, and if the spell requires concentration, you can concentrate.\n\n• Up to 5 magic potions. No more than 2 duplicate potions can be stored at a time.\n\nYou may have more than one kind of resource in the vial, up to the limits expressed above. You can use a bonus action to consume one day of food (or alcohol) or activate one scroll or magic potion. If activating a magic scroll, the effects of that scroll must end before you can activate another scroll from the Vial of Greed."},
  ["item.vial-of-stardust.wdmm2014"]={title="Vial of Stardust",subtitle="Item - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 251\n\nRaridade: unknown\n\nAny creature that sprinkles the contents of a Vial of Stardust over itself gains the ability to cast the dream spell once as an action (spell save 15), requiring no components."},
  ["magicitem.vial-of-thought-capture.azfyt2014"]={title="Vial of Thought Capture",subtitle="Item Magico - AZfyT - 2014",body="Pagina: 4\n\nRaridade: unknown (magic)\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nThis dark blue vial allows you to read another's surface thoughts and capture them as thought strands, storing the strands within the vial. As an action, you can activate the vial to target a creature you can see within 10 feet of you to learn its surface thoughts and pull the thoughts learned out of the creature's head as a tangible glowing string of energy known as a thought strand. The strands can be stored in the vial for up to 24 hours or until the vial reaches capacity, in which case the oldest strands dissipate. A creature affected by the vial knows that its thoughts are being probed.\n\nThe vial can also store thought strands created by the ggr cantrip. It does not extend the duration of those strands beyond 8 hours, but stored strands do not disappear if you cast ggr again during the duration of the cantrip.\n\nThe vial has 3 charges and can store up to 3 thought strands. It regains all its charges daily at dusk."},
  ["creature.viari.ai2014"]={title="Viari",subtitle="Criatura - AI - 2014",body="Pagina: 198\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 18/19\n\nPV: 65 (10d8 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 20 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 8 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Thieves' cant\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEvasion\n\nIf Viari is subjected to an effect that allows him to make a Dexterity saving throw to take only half damage, he instead takes no damage if he succeeds on the saving throw, and only half damage if he fails. He can't use this trait if he's incapacitated.\n\nSecond-Story Work\n\nClimbing does not cost Viari extra movement. Additionally, when he makes a running jump, the distance he covers increases by 5 feet.\n\nSneak Attack (1/Turn)\n\nViari deals an extra 14 (4d6) damage when he hits a target with a weapon attack and has advantage on the attack roll, or when the target is within 5 feet of an ally of Viari that isn't incapacitated and Viari doesn't have disadvantage on the attack roll.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nViari makes two attacks with his shortsword and two attacks with his rapier.\n\n+1 Shortsword\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d6 + 6) piercing damage.\n\nRapier\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h7 (1d4 + 5) piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nUncanny Dodge\n\nViari halves the damage that he takes from an attack that hits him. He must be able to see the attacker."},
  ["spell.vicious-mockery.phb2014"]={title="Vicious Mockery",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 285\n\nYou unleash a string of insults laced with subtle enchantments at a creature you can see within range. If the target can hear you (though it need not understand you), it must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or take 1d4 psychic damage and have disadvantage on the next attack roll it makes before the end of its next turn.\n\nThis spell's damage increases by 1d4 when you reach 5th level (2d4), 11th level (3d4), and 17th level (4d4)."},
  ["spell.vicious-mockery.xphb2024"]={title="Vicious Mockery",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 337\n\nYou unleash a string of insults laced with subtle enchantments at one creature you can see or hear within range. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or take 1d6 Psychic damage and have XPHB on the next attack roll it makes before the end of its next turn."},
  ["traphazard.vicious-vine.xdmg2024"]={title="Vicious Vine",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 78\n\nVicious vines are animated by magic. They often cling to doorways, archways, walls, and statuary. Until a vicious vine moves, there's nothing to distinguish it from an inanimate vine.\n\nEach vicious vine has AC 11; HP 16; and Immunity to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Psychic damage. When a creature enters a space within 5 feet of the vine for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, the vine tries to coil around that creature. The target must succeed on a 12 Dexterity saving throw or have the XPHB condition (escape 12). While Grappled in this way, the target takes 5 (1d10) Necrotic damage from the vine's life-draining thorns at the start of each of the target's turns. The vine can grapple only one creature at a time.\n\nAs an XPHB action, a character under the effect of a XPHB spell or similar magic can try to persuade the vine to release its victim, doing so with a successful 10 Charisma (XPHB) check. A creature released by the vine in this way won't be attacked by that vine again for the next 24 hours.\n\nAt Higher Levels\n\nYou can scale the hazard for higher levels by increasing the Necrotic damage, the save DC, and the escape DC, as shown in the following table.\n\nLevels | Necrotic Damage | Save/Escape DC\n\n5–10 | 11 (2d10) | 14\n\n11–16 | 22 (4d10) | 16\n\n17–20 | 55 (10d10) | 18"},
  ["creature.viconia-devir.mabjov2014"]={title="Viconia DeVir",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 126\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 135 (30d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 14 | WIS 20 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Elvish\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nViconia has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put Viconia to sleep.\n\nLiving Shadow\n\nWhile in dim light or darkness, Viconia has resistance to damage that isn't force, psychic, or radiant.\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nViconia wears a belt of giant strength (fire) and a cloak of protection and wields a +3 mace. Without the belt, her strength is 12 and her speed is reduced to 20 ft.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, Viconia has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nViconia attacks twice with her Magic Mace and uses her Spellcasting action.\n\nMagic Mace\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (1d6 + 10) bludgeoning damage plus 9 (2d8) necrotic damage.\n\nSacred Cleansing {@recharge 4}\n\nEach creature in a 10-foot-radius, 40-foot-high cylinder centered on a point within 60 feet must make a 18 Dexterity saving throw. A creature takes 28 (8d6) fire damage plus 28 (8d6) radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.victor-vallakovich.cos2014"]={title="Victor Vallakovich",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 105\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.victoro-cassalanter.wdh2014"]={title="Victoro Cassalanter",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 218\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 97 (15d8 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 13 | CON 14 | INT 16 | WIS 17 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Elvish, Infernal\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nVictoro wears a ring of protection and glamoured studded leather disguised to look like fine clothing. He carries a rod of rulership shaped like a ruby-tipped cane.\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nVictoro has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put him to sleep.\n\nRod of Rulership\n\nVictoro can use an action to present the rod and command obedience from each creature of his choice that he can see within 120 feet of him. Each target must succeed on a 15 Wisdom saving throw or be charmed for 8 hours by Victoro. While charmed in this way, the creature regards Victoro as its trusted leader. If harmed by Victoro or his companions, or commanded to do something contrary to its nature, a target ceases to be charmed in this way. The rod can't be used again until the next dawn.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nVictoro makes two attacks with his rapier.\n\nRapier\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d8 + 1) piercing damage.\n\nCloak of Shadows (2/Day)\n\nVictoro becomes invisible until the end of his next turn. He becomes visible early immediately after he attacks or casts a spell.\n\nSummon Devil (Recharges after 9 Days)\n\nVictoro summons a barbed devil. The devil appears in an unoccupied space within 30 feet of Victoro, acts as Victoro's ally, and can't summon other devils. It remains for 1 minute, until it or Victoro dies, or until Victoro dismisses it as an action."},
  ["feature.vigilant-blessing.tce2014.cleric.twilight.1"]={title="Vigilant Blessing",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n1st-level Twilight Domain feature\n\nThe night has taught you to be vigilant. As an action, you give one creature you touch (including possibly yourself) advantage on the next initiative roll the creature makes. This benefit ends immediately after the roll or if you use this feature again."},
  ["feature.vigilant-defender.xge2024.fighter.cavalier.18"]={title="Vigilant Defender",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 30\n\nStarting at 18th level, you respond to danger with extraordinary vigilance. In combat, you get a special reaction that you can take once on every creature's turn, except your turn. You can use this special reaction only to make an opportunity attack, and you can't use it on the same turn that you take your normal reaction."},
  ["feature.vigilant-rebuke.tce2014.paladin.watchers.15"]={title="Vigilant Rebuke",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["magicitem.vigilant-rod-of-the-honed-mind.au2014"]={title="Vigilant Rod of the Honed Mind",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 133\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias"},
  ["feat.vigor-of-the-hill-giant.bgg2014"]={title="Vigor of the Hill Giant",subtitle="Feat - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 19\n\nYou've manifested the resilience emblematic of hill giants, granting you the following benefits:\n\n• Bulwark When you are subjected to an effect that would move you at least 5 feet or give you the prone condition, you can use your reaction to steady yourself. You aren't moved and don't have the prone condition.\n\n• Iron Stomach Whenever you eat food as part of a short rest and spend one or more Hit Dice to regain hit points, you regain additional hit points equal to your Constitution modifier + your proficiency bonus."},
  ["creature.viktor.mabjov2014"]={title="Viktor",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 82\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 178 (21d8 + 84)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 12 | CON 18 | INT 11 | WIS 11 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBrave\n\nViktor has advantage on saving throws against being frightened.\n\nShadow Dragon Companion\n\nViktor has a young gold shadow dragon that accompanies him at all times. If Viktor dies, the young gold shadow dragon returns to the Shadowfell.\n\nSun Blade\n\nViktor wields a sun blade. Viktor gains a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this weapon, which deals radiant damage instead of slashing damage (this is already factored into Viktor's stat block). When Viktor hits an Undead creature with this sword, that target takes an extra 4 (1d8) radiant damage. The sword's luminous blade emits bright light in a 15-foot radius and dim light for an additional 15 feet. The light is sunlight.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nViktor makes two Sun Blade attacks and one Raven's Whisper attack.\n\nSun Blade\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (1d8 + 6) radiant damage or 11 (1d10 + 6) radiant damage if used with two hands.\n\nRaven's Whisper\n\nrs 7 to hit, range 60 ft., one target. h22 (4d10 + 3) radiant damage."},
  ["creature.viktra-mordenheim.rhw2014"]={title="Viktra Mordenheim",subtitle="Criatura - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 132\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 123 (19d8 + 38)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 21 | WIS 10 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Dwarvish, Elvish, Goblin, Halfling\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBolster Inventions\n\nAt the end of each of Viktra's turns, each of her Construct allies in a 5-foot XPHB originating from Viktra gains 5 XPHB. This trait doesn't function if Viktra has the XPHB condition.\n\nDarklord Restoration\n\nIf Viktra dies, she revives with all her XPHB in 1d10 weeks somewhere in Lamordia.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Domain)\n\nIf Viktra fails a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nActivate Constructs (1/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nViktra makes two Lightning Rod attacks. She can replace one attack with a use of Syringe.\n\nLightning Rod\n\nm,r 6, reach 5 ft. or range 90 ft. h12 (2d8 + 3) Lightning damage, and the target can't take Reactions until the start of its next turn.\n\nSyringe\n\ncon 16, one creature Viktra can see within 5 feet. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition for 1 minute. While XPHB in this way, the target suffers one of the following effects (Viktra's choice). The target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. The target succeeds automatically after 1 minute:\n\n• Corrosive Serum The target takes 10 (4d4) Acid damage at the start of each of its turns, and its XPHB decreases by 10 feet.\n\n• Deadly Serum The target takes 11 (2d10) Necrotic damage at the start of each of its turns, and it can't regain XPHB.\n\n• Mind-Altering Serum The target takes 10 (3d6) Psychic damage at the start of each of its turns, and it has XPHB on saving throws to maintain XPHB.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nRedirect Attack\n\nactTrigger A creature Viktra can see makes an attack roll against her. actResponse Viktra chooses a Small or Medium ally within 5 feet of herself. Viktra and that ally swap places, and the ally becomes the target of the attack instead.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nShocking Prod\n\nViktra moves up to half her XPHB and makes one Lightning Rod attack. Viktra can't take this action again until the start of her next turn.\n\nStatic Explosion\n\ndex 16, each creature in a 10-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point Viktra can see within 90 feet. actSaveFail 5 (2d4) Lightning damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage."},
  ["creature.viln-tirin.oota2014"]={title="Viln Tirin",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 202\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCR: 5"},
  ["creature.vilnius.cos2014"]={title="Vilnius",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 185\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.vincent-trench.wdh2014"]={title="Vincent Trench",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.vine-blight.mm2014"]={title="Vine Blight",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 26 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 8 | CON 14 | INT 5 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, deafened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the blight remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from a tangle of vines.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nConstrict\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h9 (2d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage, and a Large or smaller target is grappled (escape 12). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, and the blight can't constrict another target.\n\nEntangling Plants {@recharge 5}\n\nGrasping roots and vines sprout in a 15-foot radius centered on the blight, withering away after 1 minute. For the duration, that area is difficult terrain for nonplant creatures. In addition, each creature of the blight's choice in that area when the plants appear must succeed on a 12 Strength saving throw or become restrained. A creature can use its action to make a 12 Strength check, freeing itself or another entangled creature within reach on a success."},
  ["creature.vine-blight.xmm2024"]={title="Vine Blight",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 44\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 19 (3d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 8 | CON 14 | INT 5 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nImunidades a condicoes: deafened\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nEntangling Plants {@recharge 5}\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nConstricting Vine\n\nm 4, reach 10 ft. h6 (1d8 + 2) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 12). Until the grapple ends, the target takes 4 (1d8) Bludgeoning damage at the start of each of its turns, and the blight can't make Constricting Vine attacks."},
  ["creature.vine-blight-tangler.wtthc2014"]={title="Vine Blight Tangler",subtitle="Criatura - WttHC - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 19 (3d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 8 | CON 14 | INT 5 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nImunidades a condicoes: deafened\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nConstricting Vine\n\nm 4, reach 10 ft. h1d10 + 2 Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 12) from one of three vines.\n\nEntangling Vines {@recharge 5}\n\nGrasping vines momentarily appear on each enemy in a 10-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point of the blight's choice within 60 feet of it. Each target must succeed on a 12 Strength saving throw or have the XPHB condition until the start of the blight's next turn."},
  ["creature.vinx.hotb2014"]={title="Vinx",subtitle="Criatura - HotB - 2014",body="Pagina: 12\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 13 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Dwarvish\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nVinx makes two attacks, using Shortsword and Sling in any combination.\n\nShortsword\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage.\n\nSling\n\nr 4, range 30/120 ft. h4 (1d4 + 2) Bludgeoning damage."},
  ["item.viol.phb2014"]={title="Viol",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 154\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.viol.xphb2024"]={title="Viol",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 221\n\nRaridade: none\n\n• Ability: Charisma\n\n• Utilize: Play a known tune (10), or improvise a song (15)"},
  ["feature.violent-attraction.egw2014.wizard.graviturgy.10"]={title="Violent Attraction",subtitle="Caracteristica - EGW - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.violet-fungus.dosi2014"]={title="Violet Fungus",subtitle="Criatura - DoSI - 2014",body="Pagina: 48\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.violet-fungus.mm2014"]={title="Violet Fungus",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 138\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 5\n\nPV: 18 (4d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5\n\nSTR 3 | DEX 1 | CON 10 | INT 1 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, deafened, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the violet fungus remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from an ordinary fungus.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe fungus makes 1d4 Rotting Touch attacks.\n\nRotting Touch\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 10 ft., one creature. h4 (1d8) necrotic damage."},
  ["creature.violet-fungus.wtthc2014"]={title="Violet Fungus",subtitle="Criatura - WttHC - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.violet-fungus.xmm2024"]={title="Violet Fungus",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 126\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 5\n\nPV: 18 (4d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5\n\nSTR 3 | DEX 1 | CON 10 | INT 1 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft.\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe fungus makes two Rotting Touch attacks.\n\nRotting Touch\n\nm 2, reach 10 ft. h4 (1d8) Necrotic damage."},
  ["creature.violet-fungus-necrohulk.xmm2024"]={title="Violet Fungus Necrohulk",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 126\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 123 (13d10 + 52)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 12 | CON 18 | INT 7 | WIS 14 | CHA 10\n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe necrohulk makes two Rotting Slam attacks.\n\nRotting Slam\n\nm 7, reach 10 ft. h9 (1d10 + 4) Bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage.\n\nSpore Bomb {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 15, each creature in a 20-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point the necrohulk can see within 60 feet. actSaveFail 28 (8d6) Necrotic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of the necrohulk's next turn. While XPHB, the target can't regain XPHB. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nAbsorb Body\n\nstr 15, one Medium or Small creature the necrohulk can see within 5 feet. actSaveFail The target is pulled into the necrohulk's space and becomes grafted to its body. The necrohulk can have only one target grafted at a time.\n\nWhile grafted, the target has the XPHB condition and XPHB on Constitution saving throws. When the necrohulk moves, the grafted target moves with it. If the target dies while grafted, its body is destroyed, and the necrohulk regains 10 XPHB.\n\nThe grafted target or a creature within 5 feet of the necrohulk can take an action to make a 15 Strength (XPHB) check. On a successful check, the target is no longer grafted and moves to an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the necrohulk."},
  ["creature.virruza.dsotdq2014"]={title="Virruza",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.virvos-magen.nf2014"]={title="Virvos Magen",subtitle="Criatura - NF - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 110 (17d8 + 34)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 20\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 10 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: understands Common plus two other languages but can't speak\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDisintegration\n\nIf the magen dies, it disintegrates into dust, leaving behind anything it was wearing or carrying.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe magen has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe magen makes two Psychic Blast attacks.\n\nPsychic Blast\n\nm,r 6, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft. h21 (6d6) Psychic damage."},
  ["feature.visage-of-the-astral-self.tce2014.monk.astral-self.6"]={title="Visage of the Astral Self",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\n6th-level Way of the Astral Self feature\n\nYou can summon the visage of your astral self. As a bonus action, or as part of the bonus action you take to activate Arms of the Astral Self, you can spend 1 ki point to summon this visage for 10 minutes. It vanishes early if you are incapacitated or die.\n\nThe spectral visage covers your face like a helmet or mask. You determine its appearance.\n\nWhile the spectral visage is present, you gain the following benefits.\n\nAstral Sight\n\nYou can see normally in darkness, both magical and nonmagical, to a distance of 120 feet.\n\nWisdom of the Spirit\n\nYou have advantage on Wisdom (Insight) and Charisma (Intimidation) checks.\n\nWord of the Spirit\n\nWhen you speak, you can direct your words to a creature of your choice that you can see within 60 feet of you, making it so only that creature can hear you. Alternatively, you can amplify your voice so that all creatures within 600 feet can hear you."},
  ["spell.vision-of-elapsing-eons.au2014"]={title="Vision of Elapsing Eons",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 9 - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 45\n\nYou trick a creature you can see within range into believing it is watching itself and its surroundings crumble away, as if eons were passing in moments. The target must succeed on an Intelligence saving throw or take 10d12 Psychic damage and have the XPHB condition for the duration.\n\nWhile XPHB, the target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns. On a failed save, it gains 1 XPHB level. On a successful save, the spell ends. The spell ends early if someone within 5 feet of the target takes an action to shake it free from the illusion."},
  ["optionalfeature.visions-of-distant-realms.phb2014"]={title="Visions of Distant Realms",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 111\n\nYou can cast arcane eye at will, without expending a spell slot."},
  ["optionalfeature.visions-of-distant-realms.xphb2024"]={title="Visions of Distant Realms",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 157\n\nYou can cast XPHB without expending a spell slot."},
  ["feature.visions-of-the-past.phb2014.cleric.knowledge.17"]={title="Visions of the Past",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.vistana-assassin.cos2014"]={title="Vistana Assassin",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
