spell refers to your spellcasting ability. In addition, you use your Charisma modifier when setting the saving throw DC for a warlock spell you cast and when making an attack roll with one.\n\nSpell\n\nSpell\n\nSpellcasting Focus\n\nYou can use an phb as a spellcasting focus for your warlock spells.\n\nNivel 1 - Pact Magic\n\nPagina: 153\n\nThrough occult ceremony, you have formed a pact with a mysterious entity to gain magical powers. The entity is a voice in the shadows—its identity unclear—but its boon to you is concrete: the ability to cast spells. See XPHB for the rules on spellcasting. The information below details how you use those rules with Warlock spells, which appear in the spells later in the class's description.\n\nCantrips\n\nYou know two Warlock cantrips of your choice. XPHB and XPHB are recommended. Whenever you gain a Warlock level, you can replace one of your cantrips from this feature with another Warlock cantrip of your choice.\n\nWhen you reach Warlock levels 4 and 10, you learn another Warlock cantrip of your choice, as shown in the Cantrips column of the Warlock Features table.\n\nSpell Slots\n\nThe Warlock Features table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your Warlock spells of levels 1–5. The table also shows the level of those slots, all of which are the same level. You regain all expended Pact Magic spell slots when you finish a XPHB or XPHB.\n\nFor example, when you're a level 5 Warlock, you have two level 3 spell slots. To cast the level 1 spell XPHB, you must spend one of those slots, and you cast it as a level 3 spell.\n\nPrepared Spells of Level 1+\n\nYou prepare the list of level 1+ spells that are available for you to cast with this feature. To start, choose two level 1 Warlock spells. XPHB and XPHB are recommended.\n\nThe number of spells on your list increases as you gain Warlock levels, as shown in the Prepared Spells column of the Warlock Features table. Whenever that number increases, choose additional Warlock spells until the number of spells on your list matches the number in the table. The chosen spells must be of a level no higher than what's shown in the table's Slot Level column for your level. When you reach level 6, for example, you learn a new Warlock spell, which can be of levels 1–3.\n\nIf another Warlock feature gives you spells that you always have prepared, those spells don't count against the number of spells you can prepare with this feature, but those spells otherwise count as Warlock spells for you.\n\nChanging Your Prepared Spells\n\nWhenever you gain a Warlock level, you can replace one spell on your list with another Warlock spell of an eligible level.\n\nSpellcasting Ability\n\nCharisma is the spellcasting ability for your Warlock spells.\n\nSpellcasting Focus\n\nYou can use an XPHB as a XPHB for your Warlock spells.\n\nNivel 2 - Eldritch Invocations\n\nPagina: 105\n\nIn your study of occult lore, you have unearthed eldritch invocations, fragments of forbidden knowledge that imbue you with an abiding magical ability.\n\nAt 2nd level, you gain two eldritch invocations of your choice. A list of the available options can be found on the optionalfeatures page. When you gain certain warlock levels, you gain additional invocations of your choice, as shown in the Invocations Known column of the Warlock table.\n\nAdditionally, when you gain a level in this class, you can choose one of the invocations you know and replace it with another invocation that you could learn at that level.\n\nIf an eldritch invocation has prerequisites, you must meet them to learn it. You can learn the invocation at the same time that you meet its prerequisites. A level prerequisite refers to your level in this class.\n\nNivel 2 - Eldritch Invocations\n\nIn your study of occult lore, you have unearthed eldritch invocations, fragments of forbidden knowledge that imbue you with an abiding magical ability.\n\nAt 2nd level, you gain two eldritch invocations of your choice. Your invocation options are detailed at the end of the class description. When you gain certain warlock levels, you gain additional invocations of your choice, as shown in the Invocations Known column of the Warlock table.\n\nAdditionally, when you gain a level in this class, you can choose one of the invocations you know and replace it with another invocation that you could learn at that level.\n\nIf an eldritch invocation has prerequisites, you must meet them to learn it. You can learn the invocation at the same time that you meet its prerequisites. A level prerequisite refers to your level in this class.\n\nNivel 2 - Magical Cunning\n\nPagina: 154\n\nYou can perform an esoteric rite for 1 minute. At the end of it, you regain expended Pact Magic spell slots but no more than a number equal to half your maximum (round up). Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 2 - Magical Cunning\n\nNivel 3 - Pact Boon\n\nPagina: 105\n\nAt 3rd level, your otherworldly patron bestows a gift upon you for your loyal service. You gain one of the following features of your choice.\n\nNivel 3 - Pact Boon\n\nNivel 3 - Warlock Subclass\n\nPagina: 154\n\nYou gain a Warlock subclass of your choice. A subclass is a specialization that grants you features at certain Warlock levels. For the rest of your career, you gain each of your subclass's features that are of your Warlock level or lower.\n\nNivel 4 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 105\n\nWhen you reach 4th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 4 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 155\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify. You gain this feature again at Warlock levels 8, 12, and 16.\n\nNivel 4 - Eldritch Versatility\n\nPagina: 70\n\n{@i 4th-level warlock tce\n\nWhenever you reach a level in this class that grants the Ability Score Improvement feature, you can do one of the following, representing a change of focus in your occult studies:\n\n• Replace one cantrip you learned from this class's Pact Magic feature with another cantrip from the spells.\n\n• Replace the option you chose for the Pact Boon feature with one of that feature's other options.\n\n• If you're 12th level or higher, replace one spell from your Mystic Arcanum feature with another warlock spell of the same level.\n\nIf this change makes you ineligible for any of your Eldritch Invocations, you must also replace them now, choosing invocations for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 6 - Otherworldly Patron feature\n\nPagina: 105\n\nAt 6th level, you gain a feature granted by your Otherworldly Patron.\n\nNivel 6 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 155\n\nYou gain a feature from your Warlock subclass.\n\nNivel 8 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 105\n\nWhen you reach 8th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 8 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 155\n\nYou gain the XPHB Feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 9 - Contact Patron\n\nPagina: 155\n\nIn the past, you usually contacted your patron through intermediaries. Now you can communicate directly; you always have the XPHB spell prepared. With this feature, you can cast the spell without expending a spell slot to contact your patron, and you automatically succeed on the spell's saving throw.\n\nOnce you cast the spell with this feature, you can't do so in this way again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 10 - Otherworldly Patron feature\n\nPagina: 105\n\nAt 10th level, you gain a feature granted by your Otherworldly Patron.\n\nNivel 10 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 155\n\nYou gain a feature from your Warlock subclass.\n\nNivel 11 - Mystic Arcanum\n\nPagina: 155\n\nYour patron grants you a magical secret called an arcanum. Choose one level 6 Warlock spell as this arcanum.\n\nYou can cast your arcanum spell once without expending a spell slot, and you must finish a XPHB before you can cast it in this way again.\n\nAs shown in the Warlock Features table, you gain another Warlock spell of your choice that can be cast in this way when you reach Warlock levels 13 (level 7 spell), 15 (level 8 spell), and 17 (level 9 spell). You regain all uses of your Mystic Arcanum when you finish a XPHB.\n\nWhenever you gain a Warlock level, you can replace one of your arcanum spells with another Warlock spell of the same level.\n\nNivel 11 - Mystic Arcanum (6th level)\n\nPagina: 105\n\nAt 11th level, your patron bestows upon you a magical secret called an arcanum. Choose one spells as this arcanum.\n\nYou can cast your arcanum spell once without expending a spell slot. You must finish a long rest before you can do so again.\n\nAt higher levels, you gain more warlock spells of your choice that can be cast in this way: one 7th-level spell at 13th level, one 8th-level spell at 15th level, and one 9th-level spell at 17th level. You regain all uses of your Mystic Arcanum when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 12 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 105\n\nWhen you reach 12th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 12 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 155\n\nYou gain the XPHB Feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 13 - Mystic Arcanum\n\nPagina: 155\n\nYou gain a level 7 Warlock Spell of your choice.\n\nNivel 13 - Mystic Arcanum\n\nNivel 13 - Mystic Arcanum (7th level)\n\nPagina: 105\n\nAt 13th level, your patron bestows upon you a magical secret called an arcanum. Choose one spells as this arcanum.\n\nYou can cast your arcanum spell once without expending a spell slot. You must finish a long rest before you can do so again.\n\nNivel 14 - Otherworldly Patron feature\n\nPagina: 105\n\nAt 14th level, you gain a feature granted by your Otherworldly Patron.\n\nNivel 14 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 155\n\nYou gain a feature from your Warlock subclass.\n\nNivel 15 - Mystic Arcanum\n\nPagina: 155\n\nYou gain a level 8 Warlock Spell of your choice.\n\nNivel 15 - Mystic Arcanum\n\nNivel 15 - Mystic Arcanum (8th level)\n\nPagina: 105\n\nAt 15th level, your patron bestows upon you a magical secret called an arcanum. Choose one spells as this arcanum.\n\nYou can cast your arcanum spell once without expending a spell slot. You must finish a long rest before you can do so again.\n\nNivel 16 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 105\n\nWhen you reach 16th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 16 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 155\n\nYou gain the XPHB Feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 17 - Mystic Arcanum\n\nPagina: 155\n\nYou gain a level 9 Warlock Spell of your choice.\n\nNivel 17 - Mystic Arcanum\n\nNivel 17 - Mystic Arcanum (9th level)\n\nPagina: 105\n\nAt 17th level, your patron bestows upon you a magical secret called an arcanum. Choose one spells as this arcanum.\n\nYou can cast your arcanum spell once without expending a spell slot. You must finish a long rest before you can do so again.\n\nNivel 19 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 105\n\nWhen you reach 19th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 19 - Epic Boon\n\nPagina: 155\n\nYou gain an feats or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify. XPHB is recommended.\n\nNivel 19 - Epic Boon\n\nNivel 20 - Eldritch Master\n\nPagina: 105\n\nAt 20th level, you can draw on your inner reserve of mystical power while entreating your patron to regain expended spell slots. You can spend 1 minute entreating your patron for aid to regain all your expended spell slots from your Pact Magic feature. Once you regain spell slots with this feature, you must finish a long rest before you can do so again.\n\nNivel 20 - Eldritch Master\n\nPagina: 155\n\nWhen you use your Magical Cunning feature, you regain all your expended Pact Magic spell slots.\n\nNivel 20 - Eldritch Master"},
  ["creature.warlock-of-the-archfey.mpmm2014"]={title="Warlock of the Archfey",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 255\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 13/16\n\nPV: 67 (15d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 16 | CON 11 | INT 11 | WIS 12 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any two languages (usually Sylvan)\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe warlock makes two Rapier attacks, or it uses Bewildering Word twice.\n\nRapier\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) force damage.\n\nBewildering Word\n\nThe warlock utters a magical bewilderment, targeting one creature it can see within 60 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 14 Wisdom saving throw or take 9 (2d8) psychic damage and have disadvantage on attack rolls until the end of the warlock's next turn.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nMisty Escape (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nIn response to taking damage, the warlock turns invisible and teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space it can see. It remains invisible until the start of its next turn or until it attacks, makes a damage roll, or casts a spell."},
  ["creature.warlock-of-the-archfey.vgm2014"]={title="Warlock of the Archfey",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 219\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 11/14\n\nPV: 49 (11d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 13 | CON 11 | INT 11 | WIS 12 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any two languages (usually Sylvan)\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nMisty Escape (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nIn response to taking damage, the warlock turns invisible and teleports up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space it can see. It remains invisible until the start of its next turn or until it attacks, makes a damage roll, or casts a spell."},
  ["creature.warlock-of-the-fiend.mpmm2014"]={title="Warlock of the Fiend",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 255\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 13/16\n\nPV: 78 (12d8 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 12 | WIS 12 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: any two languages (usually Abyssal or Infernal)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDark One's Own Luck (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nWhen the warlock makes an ability check or saving throw, it can add a d10 to the roll. It can do this after the roll is made but before any of the roll's effects occur.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe warlock makes three Scimitar attacks.\n\nScimitar\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) slashing damage plus 14 (4d6) fire damage.\n\nHellfire\n\nGreen flame explodes in a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on a point within 120 feet of the warlock. Each creature in that area must make a 15 Dexterity saving throw, taking 16 (3d10) fire damage and 11 (2d10) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nFiendish Rebuke (3/Day)\n\nIn response to being damaged by a visible creature within 60 feet of it, the warlock forces that creature to make a 15 Constitution saving throw, taking 22 (4d10) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.warlock-of-the-fiend.vgm2014"]={title="Warlock of the Fiend",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 219\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 12/15\n\nPV: 78 (12d8 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 12 | WIS 12 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: any two languages (usually Abyssal or Infernal)\n\nResistencias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDark One's Own Luck (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nWhen the warlock makes an ability check or saving throw, it can add a d10 to the roll. It can do this after the roll is made but before any of the roll's effects occur.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMace\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h3 (1d6) bludgeoning damage plus 10 (3d6) fire damage."},
  ["creature.warlock-of-the-great-old-one.mpmm2014"]={title="Warlock of the Great Old One",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 256\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 13/16\n\nPV: 91 (14d8 + 28)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 12 | WIS 12 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: any two languages, telepathy 30 ft.\n\nResistencias: psychic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nWhispering Aura\n\nAt the start of each of the warlock's turns, each creature of its choice within 10 feet of it must succeed on a 15 Wisdom saving throw or take 10 (3d6) psychic damage, provided that the warlock isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe warlock makes two Dagger attacks.\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) psychic damage.\n\nHowling Void\n\nThe warlock opens a momentary extraplanar rift within 60 feet of it. The rift is a scream-filled, 20-foot cube. Each creature in that area must make a 15 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 9 (2d8) psychic damage and is frightened of the warlock until the start of the warlock's next turn. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage and isn't frightened."},
  ["creature.warlock-of-the-great-old-one.vgm2014"]={title="Warlock of the Great Old One",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 220\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 12/15\n\nPV: 91 (14d8 + 28)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 12 | WIS 12 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: any two languages, telepathy 30 ft.\n\nResistencias: psychic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nWhispering Aura\n\nAt the start of each of the warlock's turns, each creature of its choice within 5 feet of it must succeed on a 15 Wisdom saving throw or take 10 (3d6) psychic damage, provided that the warlock isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["feature.warlock-subclass.xphb2024.warlock.base.3"]={title="Warlock Subclass",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 154\n\nYou gain a Warlock subclass of your choice. A subclass is a specialization that grants you features at certain Warlock levels. For the rest of your career, you gain each of your subclass's features that are of your Warlock level or lower."},
  ["creature.warlord.mpmm2014"]={title="Warlord",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 257\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 229 (27d8 + 108)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 16 | CON 18 | INT 12 | WIS 12 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any two languages\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIndomitable (3/Day)\n\nThe warlord can reroll a saving throw it fails. It must use the new roll.\n\nSurvivor\n\nThe warlord regains 10 hit points at the start of its turn if it has fewer than half its hit points but at least 1 hit point.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe warlord makes two Greatsword or Short bow attacks.\n\nGreatsword\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nShortbow\n\nrw 7 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nCommand Ally\n\nThe warlord targets one ally it can see within 30 feet of it. If the target can see and hear the warlord, the target can make one weapon attack as a reaction and gains advantage on the attack roll.\n\nWeapon Attack\n\nThe warlord makes one Greatsword or Shortbow attack.\n\nFrighten Foe (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe warlord targets one creature it can see within 30 feet of it. If the target can see and hear it, the target must succeed on a 16 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened until the end of warlord's next turn."},
  ["creature.warlord.vgm2014"]={title="Warlord",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 220\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 229 (27d8 + 108)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 16 | CON 18 | INT 12 | WIS 12 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any two languages\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIndomitable (3/Day)\n\nThe warlord can reroll a saving throw it fails. It must use the new roll.\n\nSurvivor\n\nThe warlord regains 10 hit points at the start of its turn if it has at least 1 hit point but fewer hit points than half its hit point maximum.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe warlord makes two weapon attacks.\n\nGreatsword\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nShortbow\n\nrw 7 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nWeapon Attack\n\nThe warlord makes a weapon attack.\n\nCommand Ally\n\nThe warlord targets one ally it can see within 30 feet of it. If the target can see and hear the warlord, the target can make one weapon attack as a reaction and gains advantage on the attack roll.\n\nFrighten Foe (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe warlord targets one enemy it can see within 30 feet of it. If the target can see and hear it, the target must succeed on a 16 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened until the end of warlord's next turn."},
  ["item.warm-fungal-clothing.frhof2014"]={title="Warm Fungal Clothing",subtitle="Item - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 132\n\nRaridade: none\n\nWhen you're wearing Warm Fungal Clothing, you automatically succeed on saving throws against the effects of extreme cold. See chapter 3 of the Dungeon Master's Guide for rules on extreme cold. One pound of fungus is sewn into Fungal Clothing. This fungus can be eaten as food. Once all the fungus is consumed, this becomes a mundane set of XPHB."},
  ["spell.warp-sense.sato2014"]={title="Warp Sense",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - SatO - 2014",body="Pagina: 12\n\nFor the duration, you sense the presence of portals, even inactive ones, within 30 feet of yourself.\n\nIf you detect a portal in this way, you can use your action to study it. Make a 15 ability check using your spellcasting ability. On a successful check, you learn the destination plane of the portal and what portal key it requires, then the spell ends. On a failed check, you learn nothing and can't study that portal again using this spell until you cast it again.\n\nThe spell can penetrate most barriers but is blocked by 1 foot of stone, 1 inch of common metal, a thin sheet of lead, or 3 feet of wood or dirt."},
  ["feature.warping-implosion.tce2014.sorcerer.aberrant-mind.18"]={title="Warping Implosion",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.warping-implosion.xphb2024.sorcerer.aberrant.18"]={title="Warping Implosion",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["creature.warrior.dc2014"]={title="Warrior",subtitle="Criatura - DC - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 78 (12d8 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 12 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, plus one of your choice\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBattle Readiness\n\nThe warrior has advantage on initiative rolls.\n\nImproved Critical\n\nThe warrior's attack rolls score a critical hit on a roll of 19 or 20 on the d20.\n\nImproved Defense\n\nThe warrior's AC increases by 1.\n\nIndomitable (1/Day)\n\nThe warrior can reroll a saving throw that it fails, but it must use the new result.\n\nMartial Role\n\nThe warrior has one of the following traits of your choice:\n\n• Attacker The warrior gains a +2 bonus to attack rolls.\n\n• Defender The warrior gains the Protection reaction below.\n\nSecond Wind (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe warrior can use a bonus action on its turn to regain hit points equal to 1d10 + its level.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nExtra Attack\n\nThe warrior can attack three times, instead of once, whenever it takes the attack action on its turn.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) slashing damage, or 9 (1d10 + 4) slashing damage if used with two hands.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 6 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nProtection (Defender Only)\n\nWhen a creature the warrior can see attacks a target other than the warrior that is within 5 feet of the warrior, the warrior can use their reaction to impose disadvantage on the attack roll. The warrior must be wielding a shield."},
  ["creature.warrior.esk2014"]={title="Warrior",subtitle="Criatura - ESK - 2014",body="Pagina: 63\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 13 (2d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 13 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 12 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, plus one of your choice\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMartial Role\n\nThe warrior has one of the following traits of your choice:\n\n• Attacker\n\n• Defender\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) slashing damage, or 7 (1d10 + 2) slashing damage if used with two hands.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 3 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h5 (1d8 + 1) piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nProtection (Defender Only)\n\nThe warrior imposes disadvantage on the attack roll of a creature within 5 feet of it whose target isn't the warrior. The warrior must be able to see the attacker."},
  ["creature.warrior.sdw2014"]={title="Warrior",subtitle="Criatura - SDW - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 65 (10d8 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 12 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, plus one of your choice\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBattle Readiness\n\nThe warrior has advantage on initiative rolls.\n\nImproved Critical\n\nThe warrior's attack rolls score a critical hit on a roll of 19 or 20 on the d20.\n\nIndomitable (1/Day)\n\nThe warrior can reroll a saving throw that it fails, but it must use the new result.\n\nMartial Role\n\nThe warrior has one of the following traits of your choice:\n\n• Attacker The warrior gains a +2 bonus to attack rolls.\n\n• Defender The warrior gains the Protection reaction below.\n\nSecond Wind (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe warrior can use a bonus action on its turn to regain hit points equal to 1d10 + its level.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nExtra Attack\n\nThe warrior can attack twice, instead of once, whenever it takes the attack action on its turn.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) slashing damage, or 9 (1d10 + 4) slashing damage if used with two hands.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 6 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nProtection (Defender Only)\n\nWhen a creature the warrior can see attacks a target other than the warrior that is within 5 feet of the warrior, the warrior can use their reaction to impose disadvantage on the attack roll. The warrior must be wielding a shield."},
  ["creature.warrior.slw2014"]={title="Warrior",subtitle="Criatura - SLW - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 52 (8d8 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 12 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, plus one of your choice\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBattle Readiness\n\nThe warrior has advantage on initiative rolls.\n\nImproved Critical\n\nThe warrior's attack rolls score a critical hit on a roll of 19 or 20 on the d20.\n\nMartial Role\n\nThe warrior has one of the following traits of your choice:\n\n• Attacker\n\n• Defender\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nExtra Attack\n\nThe warrior can attack twice, instead of once, whenever it takes the Attack action on its turn.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) slashing damage, or 8 (1d10 + 3) slashing damage if used with two hands.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nProtection (Defender Only)\n\nThe warrior imposes disadvantage on the attack roll of a creature within 5 feet of it whose target isn't the warrior. The warrior must be able to see the attacker."},
  ["creature.warrior-commander.xmm2024"]={title="Warrior Commander",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 321\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 161 (19d8 + 76)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 20 | CON 18 | INT 14 | WIS 16 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus one other language\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe warrior makes three attacks, using Greatsword or Longbow in any combination.\n\nGreatsword\n\nm 9, reach 5 ft. h19 (4d6 + 5) Slashing damage. The warrior also creates one of the following effects:\n\n• Sap The target has XPHB on its next attack roll before the start of the warrior's next turn.\n\n• Maneuver One ally who can see or hear the warrior can take a XPHB to move up to half the ally's XPHB without provoking XPHB.\n\nLongbow\n\nr 9, range 150/600 ft. h18 (3d8 + 5) Piercing damage, and the target's XPHB decreases by 10 feet until the end of the target's next turn.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nTactical Charge\n\nThe warrior moves up to half its XPHB straight toward an enemy it can see without provoking XPHB.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nCounterattack\n\nactTrigger The warrior is hit by an attack roll. actResponse The warrior adds 4 to its AC against that attack, possibly causing it to miss. On a miss, the warrior can make one Greatsword or Longbow attack against the attacker."},
  ["creature.warrior-infantry.xmm2024"]={title="Warrior Infantry",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 320\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 9 (2d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 11 | CON 11 | INT 8 | WIS 11 | CHA 8\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe warrior has XPHB on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the warrior's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally doesn't have the XPHB condition.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSpear\n\nm,r 3, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. h4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage."},
  ["creature.warrior-of-madarua.qftis2014"]={title="Warrior of Madarua",subtitle="Criatura - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 220\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 12 | CON 13 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nThe warrior adds 2 to its AC against one melee attack that would hit it. To do so, the warrior must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon."},
  ["subclass.warrior-of-mercy.xphb2024.monk.mercy.0"]={title="Warrior of Mercy",subtitle="Subclasse - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 104\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Hand of Harm\n\nPagina: 49\n\n3rd-level Way of Mercy feature\n\nYou use your ki to inflict wounds. When you hit a creature with an unarmed strike, you can spend 1 ki point to deal extra necrotic damage equal to one roll of your Martial Arts die + your Wisdom modifier. You can use this feature only once per turn.\n\nNivel 3 - Hand of Harm\n\nPagina: 104\n\nOnce per turn when you hit a creature with an XPHB and deal damage, you can expend 1 Focus Point to deal extra Necrotic damage equal to one roll of your Martial Arts die plus your Wisdom modifier.\n\nNivel 3 - Hand of Harm\n\nNivel 3 - Hand of Healing\n\nPagina: 49\n\n3rd-level Way of Mercy feature\n\nYour mystical touch can mend wounds. As an action, you can spend 1 ki point to touch a creature and restore a number of hit points equal to a roll of your Martial Arts die + your Wisdom modifier.\n\nWhen you use your Flurry of Blows, you can replace one of the unarmed strikes with a use of this feature without spending a ki point for the healing.\n\nNivel 3 - Hand of Healing\n\nPagina: 104\n\nAs a XPHB action, you can expend 1 Focus Point to touch a creature and restore a number of XPHB equal to a roll of your Martial Arts die plus your Wisdom modifier. When you use your Flurry of Blows, you can replace one of the Unarmed Strikes with a use of this feature without expending a Focus Point for the healing.\n\nNivel 3 - Hand of Healing\n\nNivel 3 - Implements of Mercy\n\nPagina: 49\n\n3rd-level Way of Mercy feature\n\nYou gain proficiency in the Insight and Medicine skills, and you gain proficiency with the PHB.\n\nYou also gain a special mask, which you often wear when using the features of this subclass. You determine its appearance, or generate it randomly by rolling on the Merciful Mask table.\n\nd6 | Mask Appearance\n\n1 | Raven\n\n2 | Blank and white\n\n3 | Crying visage\n\n4 | Laughing visage\n\n5 | Skull\n\n6 | Butterfly\n\nNivel 3 - Implements of Mercy\n\nPagina: 104\n\nYou gain proficiency in the XPHB and XPHB skills and proficiency with the XPHB.\n\nNivel 3 - Implements of Mercy\n\nNivel 3 - Warrior of Mercy\n\nPagina: 104\n\nManipulate Forces of Life and Death\n\nWarriors of Mercy manipulate the life force of others. These Monks are wandering physicians, but they bring a swift end to their enemies. They often wear masks, presenting themselves as faceless bringers of life and death.\n\nNivel 3 - Way of Mercy\n\nPagina: 49\n\nMonks of the Way of Mercy learn to manipulate the life force of others to bring aid to those in need. They are wandering physicians to the poor and hurt. However, to those beyond their help, they bring a swift end as an act of mercy.\n\nThose who follow the Way of Mercy might be members of a religious order, administering to the needy and making grim choices rooted in reality rather than idealism. Some might be gentle-voiced healers, beloved by their communities, while others might be masked bringers of macabre mercies.\n\nThe walkers of this way usually don robes with deep cowls, and they often conceal their faces with masks, presenting themselves as the faceless bringers of life and death.\n\nNivel 6 - Physician's Touch\n\nPagina: 49\n\n6th-level Way of Mercy feature\n\nYou can administer even greater cures with a touch, and if you feel it's necessary, you can use your knowledge to cause harm.\n\nWhen you use Hand of Healing on a creature, you can also end one disease or one of the following conditions affecting the creature: blinded, deafened, paralyzed, poisoned, or stunned.\n\nWhen you use Hand of Harm on a creature, you can subject that creature to the poisoned condition until the end of your next turn.\n\nNivel 6 - Physician's Touch\n\nPagina: 104\n\nYour Hand of Harm and Hand of Healing improve, as detailed below.\n\nHand of Harm\n\nWhen you use Hand of Harm on a creature, you can also give that creature the XPHB condition until the end of your next turn.\n\nHand of Healing\n\nWhen you use Hand of Healing, you can also end one of the following conditions on the creature you heal: XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB.\n\nNivel 6 - Physician's Touch\n\nNivel 11 - Flurry of Healing and Harm\n\nPagina: 49\n\n11th-level Way of Mercy feature\n\nYou can now mete out a flurry of comfort and hurt. When you use Flurry of Blows, you can now replace each of the unarmed strikes with a use of your Hand of Healing, without spending ki points for the healing.\n\nIn addition, when you make an unarmed strike with Flurry of Blows, you can use Hand of Harm with that strike without spending the ki point for Hand of Harm. You can still use Hand of Harm only once per turn.\n\nNivel 11 - Flurry of Healing and Harm\n\nPagina: 104\n\nWhen you use Flurry of Blows, you can replace each of the Unarmed Strikes with a use of Hand of Healing without expending Focus Points for the healing.\n\nIn addition, when you make an XPHB with Flurry of Blows and deal damage, you can use Hand of Harm with that strike without expending a Focus Point for Hand of Harm. You can still use Hand of Harm only once per turn.\n\nYou can use these benefits a total number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 17 - Hand of Ultimate Mercy\n\nPagina: 49\n\n17th-level Way of Mercy feature\n\nYour mastery of life energy opens the door to the ultimate mercy. As an action, you can touch the corpse of a creature that died within the past 24 hours and expend 5 ki points. The creature then returns to life, regaining a number of hit points equal to 4d10 + your Wisdom modifier. If the creature died while subject to any of the following conditions, it revives with them removed: blinded, deafened, paralyzed, poisoned, and stunned.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 17 - Hand of Ultimate Mercy\n\nPagina: 105\n\nYour mastery of life energy opens the door to the ultimate mercy. As a XPHB action, you can touch the corpse of a creature that died within the past 24 hours and expend 5 Focus Points. The creature then returns to life with a number of XPHB equal to 4d10 plus your Wisdom modifier. If the creature died with any of the following conditions, the creature revives with the conditions removed: XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 17 - Hand of Ultimate Mercy"},
  ["feature.warrior-of-mercy.xphb2024.monk.mercy.3"]={title="Warrior of Mercy",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 104\n\nManipulate Forces of Life and Death\n\nWarriors of Mercy manipulate the life force of others. These Monks are wandering physicians, but they bring a swift end to their enemies. They often wear masks, presenting themselves as faceless bringers of life and death."},
  ["subclass.warrior-of-shadow.xphb2024.monk.shadow.0"]={title="Warrior of Shadow",subtitle="Subclasse - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 105\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Darkness\n\nPagina: 105\n\nYou can expend 1 Focus Point to cast the XPHB spell without spell components. You can see within the spell's area when you cast it with this feature. While the spell persists, you can move its area of XPHB to a space within 60 feet of yourself at the start of each of your turns.\n\nNivel 3 - Darkness\n\nNivel 3 - Darkvision\n\nPagina: 105\n\nYou gain XPHB with a range of 60 feet. If you already have XPHB, its range increases by 60 feet.\n\nNivel 3 - Darkvision\n\nNivel 3 - Shadow Arts\n\nPagina: 80\n\nYou can use your ki to duplicate the effects of certain spells. As an action, you can spend 2 ki points to cast darkness, darkvision, pass without trace, or silence, without providing material components. Additionally, you gain the minor illusion cantrip if you don't already know it.\n\nNivel 3 - Shadow Arts\n\nPagina: 105\n\nYou have learned to draw on the power of the Shadowfell, gaining the following benefits.\n\nNivel 3 - Shadowy Figments\n\nPagina: 105\n\nYou know the XPHB spell. Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for it.\n\nNivel 3 - Warrior of Shadow\n\nPagina: 105\n\nHarness Shadow Power for Stealth and Subterfuge\n\nWarriors of Shadow practice stealth and subterfuge, harnessing the power of the Shadowfell. They are at home in darkness, able to draw gloom around themselves to hide, leap from shadow to shadow, and take on a wraithlike form.\n\nNivel 3 - Way of Shadow\n\nPagina: 80\n\nMonks of the Way of Shadow follow a tradition that values stealth and subterfuge. These monks might be called ninjas or shadow dancers, and they serve as spies and assassins. Sometimes the members of a ninja monastery are family members, forming a clan sworn to secrecy about their arts and missions. Other monasteries are more like thieves' guilds, hiring out their services to nobles, rich merchants, or anyone else who can pay their fees. Regardless of their methods, the heads of these monasteries expect the unquestioning obedience of their students.\n\nNivel 6 - Shadow Step\n\nPagina: 80\n\nYou gain the ability to step from one shadow into another. When you are in dim light or darkness, as a bonus action you can teleport up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space you can see that is also in dim light or darkness. You then have advantage on the first melee attack you make before the end of the turn.\n\nNivel 6 - Shadow Step\n\nPagina: 105\n\nWhile entirely within XPHB or XPHB, you can use a XPHB to teleport up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space you can see that is also in XPHB or XPHB. You then have XPHB on the next melee attack you make before the end of the current turn.\n\nNivel 6 - Shadow Step\n\nNivel 6 - Shadow Step\n\nNivel 11 - Cloak of Shadows\n\nPagina: 80\n\nBy 11th level, you have learned to become one with the shadows. When you are in an area of dim light or darkness, you can use your action to become invisible. You remain invisible until you make an attack, cast a spell, or are in an area of bright light.\n\nNivel 11 - Improved Shadow Step\n\nPagina: 105\n\nYou can draw on your Shadowfell connection to empower your teleportation. When you use your Shadow Step, you can expend 1 Focus Point to remove the requirement that you must start and end in XPHB or XPHB for that use of the feature. As part of this XPHB, you can make an XPHB immediately after you teleport.\n\nNivel 11 - Improved Shadow Step\n\nNivel 17 - Cloak of Shadows\n\nPagina: 105\n\nAs a XPHB action while entirely within XPHB or XPHB, you can expend 3 Focus Points to shroud yourself with shadows for 1 minute, until you have the XPHB condition, or until you end your turn in XPHB. While shrouded by these shadows, you gain the following benefits.\n\nInvisibility\n\nYou have the XPHB condition.\n\nPartially Incorporeal\n\nYou can move through occupied spaces as if they were XPHB. If you end your turn in such a space, you are shunted to the last unoccupied space you were in.\n\nShadow Flurry\n\nYou can use your Flurry of Blows without expending any Focus Points.\n\nNivel 17 - Cloak of Shadows\n\nNivel 17 - Opportunist\n\nPagina: 80\n\nAt 17th level, you can exploit a creature's momentary distraction when it is hit by an attack. Whenever a creature within 5 feet of you is hit by an attack made by a creature other than you, you can use your reaction to make a melee attack against that creature."},
  ["feature.warrior-of-shadow.xphb2024.monk.shadow.3"]={title="Warrior of Shadow",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 105\n\nHarness Shadow Power for Stealth and Subterfuge\n\nWarriors of Shadow practice stealth and subterfuge, harnessing the power of the Shadowfell. They are at home in darkness, able to draw gloom around themselves to hide, leap from shadow to shadow, and take on a wraithlike form."},
  ["subclass.warrior-of-the-elements.xphb2024.monk.elements.0"]={title="Warrior of the Elements",subtitle="Subclasse - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 106\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Elemental Attunement\n\nPagina: 106\n\nAt the start of your turn, you can expend 1 Focus Point to imbue yourself with elemental energy. The energy lasts for 10 minutes or until you have the XPHB condition. You gain the following benefits while this feature is active.\n\nReach\n\nWhen you make an XPHB, your reach is 10 feet greater than normal, as elemental energy extends from you.\n\nElemental Strikes\n\nWhenever you hit with your XPHB, you can cause it to deal your choice of Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder damage rather than its normal damage type. When you deal one of these types with it, you can also force the target to make a Strength saving throw. On a failed save, you can move the target up to 10 feet toward or away from you, as elemental energy swirls around it.\n\nNivel 3 - Elemental Attunement\n\nNivel 3 - Manipulate Elements\n\nPagina: 106\n\nYou know the XPHB spell. Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for it.\n\nNivel 3 - Warrior of the Elements\n\nPagina: 106\n\nWield Strikes and Bursts of Elemental Power\n\nWarriors of the Elements tap into the power of the Elemental Planes. Harnessing their supernatural focus, these Monks momentarily tame the energy of the Elemental Chaos to empower themselves in and out of battle.\n\nNivel 6 - Elemental Burst\n\nPagina: 106\n\nAs a XPHB action, you can expend 2 Focus Points to cause elemental energy to burst in a 20-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point within 120 feet of yourself. Choose a damage type: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder.\n\nEach creature in the XPHB must make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes damage of the chosen type equal to three rolls of your Martial Arts die. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage.\n\nNivel 6 - Elemental Burst\n\nNivel 11 - Stride of the Elements\n\nPagina: 106\n\nWhile your Elemental Attunement is active, you also have a XPHB and a XPHB equal to your XPHB.\n\nNivel 17 - Elemental Epitome\n\nPagina: 106\n\nWhile your Elemental Attunement is active, you also gain the following benefits.\n\nDamage Resistance\n\nYou gain XPHB to one of the following damage types of your choice: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder. At the start of each of your turns, you can change this choice.\n\nDestructive Stride\n\nWhen you use your Step of the Wind, your XPHB increases by 20 feet until the end of the turn. For that duration, any creature of your choice takes damage equal to one roll of your Martial Arts die when you enter a space within 5 feet of it. The damage type is your choice of Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder. A creature can take this damage only once per turn.\n\nEmpowered Strikes\n\nOnce on each of your turns, you can deal extra damage to a target equal to one roll of your Martial Arts die when you hit it with an XPHB. The extra damage is the same type dealt by that strike.\n\nNivel 17 - Elemental Epitome"},
  ["feature.warrior-of-the-elements.xphb2024.monk.elements.3"]={title="Warrior of the Elements",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 106\n\nWield Strikes and Bursts of Elemental Power\n\nWarriors of the Elements tap into the power of the Elemental Planes. Harnessing their supernatural focus, these Monks momentarily tame the energy of the Elemental Chaos to empower themselves in and out of battle."},
  ["feature.warrior-of-the-gods.xge2024.barbarian.zealot.3"]={title="Warrior of the Gods",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 11\n\nAt 3rd level, your soul is marked for endless battle. If a spell, such as raise dead, has the sole effect of restoring you to life (but not undeath), the caster doesn't need material components to cast the spell on you."},
  ["feature.warrior-of-the-gods.xphb2024.barbarian.zealot.3"]={title="Warrior of the Gods",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["subclass.warrior-of-the-mystic-arts.au2014.monk.mystic-arts.0"]={title="Warrior of the Mystic Arts",subtitle="Subclasse - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 11\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Spellcasting\n\nPagina: 11\n\nYou have learned to cast spells. See the XPHB for the rules on spellcasting. The information below details how you use those rules as a Warrior of the Mystic Arts.\n\nCantrips\n\nYou know two cantrips of your choice from the spells. XPHB and XPHB are recommended. Whenever you gain a Monk level, you can replace one of these cantrips with another cantrip of your choice from the spells.\n\nWhen you reach Monk level 10, you learn another spells of your choice.\n\nSpell Slots\n\nThe Warrior of the Mystic Arts Spellcasting table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your level 1+ spells. You regain all expended slots when you finish a XPHB.\n\nPrepared Spells of Level 1+\n\nYou prepare the list of level 1+ spells that are available for you to cast with this feature. To start, choose three level 1 spells from the spells. XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB are recommended.\n\nThe number of spells on your list increases as you gain Monk levels, as shown in the Prepared Spells column of the Warrior of the Mystic Arts Spellcasting table. Whenever that number increases, choose additional spells from the spells until the number of spells on your list matches the number on the table. The chosen spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots. For example, if you're a level 7 Monk, your list of prepared spells can include five Sorcerer spells of levels 1 and 2 in any combination.\n\nChanging Your Prepared Spells\n\nWhenever you gain a Monk level, you can replace one spell on your list with another spells for which you have spell slots.\n\nSpellcasting Ability\n\nWisdom is your spellcasting ability for your Sorcerer spells.\n\nSpellcasting Focus\n\nYou can use an XPHB as a XPHB for your Sorcerer spells.\n\nMulticlassing\n\nIf you multiclass and have the Spellcasting feature from more than one class, add one third of your Monk levels (round down) to determine your available spell slots.\n\nNivel 3 - Warrior of the Mystic Arts\n\nPagina: 11\n\nWeave Martial and Mystic Arts\n\nWarriors of the Mystic Arts wield magic to supplement their martial skill. They harness mystical focus to enhance their magical and physical abilities.\n\nNivel 6 - Mystic Fighting Style\n\nPagina: 12\n\nWhen you take the XPHB action on your turn, you can replace one XPHB with a casting of one of your Sorcerer cantrips that has a casting time of an action.\n\nNivel 6 - Mystic Focus\n\nPagina: 12\n\nYou keep your magical power and martial focus in perfect balance, allowing you to convert spell slots into Focus Points, or convert Focus Points into spell slots.\n\nConverting Spell Slots to Focus Points\n\nYou can expend a spell slot to regain a number of expended Focus Points equal to the slot's level (no action required).\n\nRecovering Spell Slots\n\nWhen you finish a XPHB or use Uncanny Metabolism, you can transform unexpended Focus Points to recover one expended spell slot. The Recovering Spell Slots table shows the cost of recovering a spell slot of a given level, and it lists the minimum Monk level you must be to recover a slot. You can recover a spell slot no higher than level 4.\n\nSpell Slot Level | Focus Point Cost | Min. Monk Level\n\n1 | 2 | 6\n\n2 | 3 | 7\n\n3 | 5 | 13\n\n4 | 6 | 19\n\nNivel 6 - Mystic Focus\n\nNivel 11 - Focused Strike\n\nPagina: 13\n\nWhen you use your Stunning Strike, whether the target succeeds or fails on the saving throw, the target has XPHB on saving throws against your spells until the start of your next turn.\n\nNivel 11 - Focused Strike\n\nNivel 17 - Improved Mystic Fighting Style\n\nPagina: 13\n\nWhen you use Flurry of Blows, you can replace two of the XPHB with a casting of one of your level 1 or 2 Sorcerer spells that has a casting time of an action, and you cast it as part of the same XPHB you use to activate Flurry of Blows."},
  ["feature.warrior-of-the-mystic-arts.au2014.monk.mystic-arts.3"]={title="Warrior of the Mystic Arts",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 11\n\nWeave Martial and Mystic Arts\n\nWarriors of the Mystic Arts wield magic to supplement their martial skill. They harness mystical focus to enhance their magical and physical abilities."},
  ["subclass.warrior-of-the-open-hand.xphb2024.monk.open-hand.0"]={title="Warrior of the Open Hand",subtitle="Subclasse - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 107\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Open Hand Technique\n\nPagina: 79\n\nYou can manipulate your enemy's ki when you harness your own. Whenever you hit a creature with one of the attacks granted by your Flurry of Blows, you can impose one of the following effects on that target.\n\n• It must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\n• It must make a Strength saving throw. If it fails, you can push it up to 15 feet away from you.\n\n• It can't take reactions until the end of your next turn.\n\nNivel 3 - Open Hand Technique\n\nPagina: 107\n\nWhenever you hit a creature with an attack granted by your Flurry of Blows, you can impose one of the following effects on that target.\n\nAddle\n\nThe target can't make XPHB until the start of its next turn.\n\nPush\n\nThe target must succeed on a Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 15 feet away from you.\n\nTopple\n\nThe target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or have the XPHB condition.\n\nNivel 3 - Open Hand Technique\n\nNivel 3 - Warrior of the Open Hand\n\nPagina: 107\n\nMaster Unarmed Combat Techniques\n\nWarriors of the Open Hand are masters of unarmed combat. They learn techniques to push and trip their opponents and manipulate their own energy to protect themselves from harm.\n\nNivel 3 - Way of the Open Hand\n\nPagina: 79\n\nMonks of the Way of the Open Hand are the ultimate masters of martial arts combat, whether armed or unarmed. They learn techniques to push and trip their opponents, manipulate ki to heal damage to their bodies, and practice advanced meditation that can protect them from harm.\n\nNivel 6 - Wholeness of Body\n\nPagina: 79\n\nYou gain the ability to heal yourself. As an action, you can regain hit points equal to three times your monk level. You must finish a long rest before you can use this feature again.\n\nNivel 6 - Wholeness of Body\n\nPagina: 107\n\nYou gain the ability to heal yourself. As a XPHB, you can roll your Martial Arts die. You regain a number of XPHB equal to the number rolled plus your Wisdom modifier (minimum of 1 XPHB regained).\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 6 - Wholeness of Body\n\nNivel 11 - Fleet Step\n\nPagina: 107\n\nWhen you take a XPHB other than Step of the Wind, you can also use Step of the Wind immediately after that XPHB.\n\nNivel 11 - Tranquility\n\nPagina: 79\n\nBeginning at 11th level, you can enter a special meditation that surrounds you with an aura of peace. At the end of a long rest, you gain the effect of a sanctuary spell that lasts until the start of your next long rest (the spell can end early as normal). The saving throw DC for the spell equals 8 + your Wisdom modifier + your proficiency bonus.\n\nNivel 17 - Quivering Palm\n\nPagina: 79\n\nYou gain the ability to set up lethal vibrations in someone's body. When you hit a creature with an unarmed strike, you can spend 3 ki points to start these imperceptible vibrations, which last for a number of days equal to your monk level. The vibrations are harmless unless you use your action to end them. To do so, you and the target must be on the same plane of existence. When you use this action, the creature must make a Constitution saving throw. If it fails, it is reduced to 0 hit points. If it succeeds, it takes 10d10 necrotic damage.\n\nYou can have only one creature under the effect of this feature at a time. You can choose to end the vibrations harmlessly without using an action.\n\nNivel 17 - Quivering Palm\n\nPagina: 107\n\nYou gain the ability to set up lethal vibrations in someone's body. When you hit a creature with an XPHB, you can expend 4 Focus Points to start these imperceptible vibrations, which last for a number of days equal to your Monk level. The vibrations are harmless unless you take an action to end them. Alternatively, when you take the XPHB action on your turn, you can forgo one of the attacks to end the vibrations. To end them, you and the target must be on the same plane of existence. When you end them, the target must make a Constitution saving throw, taking 10d12 Force damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nYou can have only one creature under the effect of this feature at a time. You can end the vibrations harmlessly (no action required).\n\nNivel 17 - Quivering Palm"},
  ["feature.warrior-of-the-open-hand.xphb2024.monk.open-hand.3"]={title="Warrior of the Open Hand",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 107\n\nMaster Unarmed Combat Techniques\n\nWarriors of the Open Hand are masters of unarmed combat. They learn techniques to push and trip their opponents and manipulate their own energy to protect themselves from harm."},
  ["class.warrior-sidekick.tce2014"]={title="Warrior Sidekick",subtitle="Classe - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 146\n\nSidekick Class|Warrior Sidekick|TCE|1\n\nBonus Proficiencies|Warrior Sidekick|TCE|1\n\nMartial Role|Warrior Sidekick|TCE|1\n\nSecond Wind|Warrior Sidekick|TCE|2\n\nImproved Critical|Warrior Sidekick|TCE|3\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Warrior Sidekick|TCE|4\n\nExtra Attack|Warrior Sidekick|TCE|6\n\nBattle Readiness|Warrior Sidekick|TCE|7\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Warrior Sidekick|TCE|8\n\nImproved Defense|Warrior Sidekick|TCE|10\n\nIndomitable|Warrior Sidekick|TCE|11\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Warrior Sidekick|TCE|12\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Warrior Sidekick|TCE|14\n\nExtra Attack Improvement|Warrior Sidekick|TCE|15\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Warrior Sidekick|TCE|16\n\nIndomitable Improvement|Warrior Sidekick|TCE|18\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Warrior Sidekick|TCE|19\n\nSecond Wind Improvement|Warrior Sidekick|TCE|20\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA CLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Bonus Proficiencies\n\nPagina: 146\n\n1st-level Warrior feature\n\nThe sidekick gains proficiency in one saving throw of your choice: Strength, Dexterity, or Constitution.\n\nIn addition, the sidekick gains proficiency in two skills of your choice from the following list: Acrobatics, Animal Handling, Athletics, Intimidation, Nature, Perception, and Survival.\n\nThe sidekick gains proficiency with all armor, and if it is a humanoid or has a items in its stat block, it gains proficiency with shields and all simple and martial weapons.\n\nNivel 1 - Bonus Proficiencies\n\nNivel 1 - Martial Role\n\nPagina: 146\n\n1st-level Warrior feature\n\nEach warrior focuses on offense or defense in their training. Choose one of the following options:\n\n• Attacker\n\n• Defender\n\nNivel 1 - Sidekick Class\n\nPagina: 146\n\n{@note Note: this class is intended for NPC tce.\n\nNivel 2 - Second Wind\n\nPagina: 146\n\n2nd-level Warrior feature\n\nThe sidekick can use a bonus action on its turn to regain hit points equal to 1d10 + its level in this class. Once it uses this feature, it must finish a short or long rest before it can use it again.\n\nThe sidekick can use this feature twice between rests starting at 20th level.\n\nNivel 3 - Improved Critical\n\nPagina: 146\n\n3rd-level Warrior feature\n\nThe sidekick's attack rolls score a critical hit on a roll of 19 or 20 on the d20.\n\nNivel 4 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 146\n\n4th-level Warrior feature\n\nAt 4th level and again at 8th, 12th, 14th, 16th, and 19th level, the sidekick increases one ability score of your choice by 2, or the sidekick increases two ability scores of your choice by 1. The sidekick can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, the sidekick may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 6 - Extra Attack\n\nPagina: 146\n\n6th-level Warrior feature\n\nThe sidekick can attack twice, instead of once, whenever it takes the Attack action on its turn.\n\nThe number of attacks increases to three when the sidekick reaches 15th level.\n\nIf the sidekick has the Multiattack action, it can use Extra Attack or Multiattack on a turn, not both.\n\nNivel 7 - Battle Readiness\n\nPagina: 146\n\n7th-level Warrior feature\n\nThe sidekick has advantage on initiative rolls.\n\nNivel 8 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 146\n\n8th-level Warrior feature\n\nAt 4th level and again at 8th, 12th, 14th, 16th, and 19th level, the sidekick increases one ability score of your choice by 2, or the sidekick increases two ability scores of your choice by 1. The sidekick can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, the sidekick may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 10 - Improved Defense\n\nPagina: 146\n\n10th-level Warrior feature\n\nThe sidekick's Armor Class increases by 1.\n\nNivel 11 - Indomitable\n\nPagina: 146\n\n11th-level Warrior feature\n\nThe sidekick can reroll a saving throw that it fails, but it must use the new roll. When it uses this feature, it can't use the feature again until it finishes a long rest.\n\nThe sidekick can use this feature twice between long rests starting at 18th level.\n\nNivel 12 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 146\n\n12th-level Warrior feature\n\nAt 4th level and again at 8th, 12th, 14th, 16th, and 19th level, the sidekick increases one ability score of your choice by 2, or the sidekick increases two ability scores of your choice by 1. The sidekick can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, the sidekick may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 14 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 146\n\n14th-level Warrior feature\n\nAt 4th level and again at 8th, 12th, 14th, 16th, and 19th level, the sidekick increases one ability score of your choice by 2, or the sidekick increases two ability scores of your choice by 1. The sidekick can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, the sidekick may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 15 - Extra Attack Improvement\n\nPagina: 146\n\n15th-level Warrior feature\n\nThe sidekick can attack twice, instead of once, whenever it takes the Attack action on its turn.\n\nThe number of attacks increases to three when the sidekick reaches 15th level.\n\nIf the sidekick has the Multiattack action, it can use Extra Attack or Multiattack on a turn, not both.\n\nNivel 16 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 146\n\n16th-level Warrior feature\n\nAt 4th level and again at 8th, 12th, 14th, 16th, and 19th level, the sidekick increases one ability score of your choice by 2, or the sidekick increases two ability scores of your choice by 1. The sidekick can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, the sidekick may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 18 - Indomitable Improvement\n\nPagina: 146\n\n18th-level Warrior feature\n\nThe sidekick can reroll a saving throw that it fails, but it must use the new roll. When it uses this feature, it can't use the feature again until it finishes a long rest.\n\nThe sidekick can use this feature twice between long rests starting at 18th level.\n\nNivel 19 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 146\n\n19th-level Warrior feature\n\nAt 4th level and again at 8th, 12th, 14th, 16th, and 19th level, the sidekick increases one ability score of your choice by 2, or the sidekick increases two ability scores of your choice by 1. The sidekick can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, the sidekick may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 20 - Second Wind Improvement\n\nPagina: 146\n\n20th-level Warrior feature\n\nThe sidekick can use its Second Wind feature twice between rests."},
  ["creature.warrior-veteran.xmm2024"]={title="Warrior Veteran",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 320\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 65 (10d8 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 13 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 11 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus one other language\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe warrior makes two Greatsword or Heavy Crossbow attacks.\n\nGreatsword\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h10 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage.\n\nHeavy Crossbow\n\nr 3, range 100/400 ft. h12 (2d10 + 1) Piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nactTrigger The warrior is hit by a melee attack roll while holding a weapon. actResponse The warrior adds 2 to its AC against that attack, possibly causing it to miss."},
  ["magicitem.warrior-s-passkey.bmt2014"]={title="Warrior's Passkey",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 39\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis silver skeleton key is warm to the touch. While holding the key in its key form, you can use an action to cast the Knock spell from the key.\n\nTransforming the Key\n\nWhile holding the key, you can use a bonus action to transform it into a magic longsword. You are considered proficient with the sword, and you have a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. On a hit, the sword deals 1d10 force damage. The item remains in its sword form until it leaves your grasp or you use another bonus action to revert it to its key form.\n\nIf you end your attunement to the item while it's in its sword form, it automatically reverts to its key form."},
  ["item.warship.dmg2014"]={title="Warship",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["vehicle.warship.gos2014"]={title="Warship",subtitle="Veiculo - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 194\n\nOn its turn, the warship can take 3 actions, choosing from the options below. It can take only 2 actions if it has fewer than twenty crew and only 1 action if it has fewer than ten. It can't take these actions if it has fewer than three crew.\n\n• Fire Ballistas\n\n• Fire Mangonels\n\n• Move"},
  ["item.warship.xphb2024"]={title="Warship",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 230\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.warwyck-blastimoff.lox2014"]={title="Warwyck Blastimoff",subtitle="Criatura - LoX - 2014",body="Pagina: 39\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["item.wasp-ship.aag2014"]={title="Wasp Ship",subtitle="Item - AAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 56\n\nRaridade: none\n\nWasp ships are lightweight wooden vessels capable of landing safely on the ground, but not on water. They appeal to adventurers because they're affordable and don't require a large crew. Pirates like them because they're swift. Aristocrats are fond of using them as flying yachts because the ship's cargo hold can be easily converted into posh living quarters.\n\nThe ship's raised back provides high ground for a weapon emplacement, which is typically equipped with a ballista."},
  ["vehicle.wasp-ship.aag2014"]={title="Wasp Ship",subtitle="Veiculo - AAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 56"},
  ["creature.wasteland-dragonnel.dsotdq2014"]={title="Wasteland Dragonnel",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 201\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 65 (10d10 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 8 | WIS 13 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common and Draconic but can't speak\n\nResistencias: acid\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlyby\n\nThe dragonnel doesn't provoke opportunity attacks when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragonnel makes two Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nAcid Spit\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 60 ft., one target. h20 (5d6 + 3) acid damage."},
  ["creature.wastrilith.mpmm2014"]={title="Wastrilith",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 258\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 157 (15d10 + 75)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 80\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 18 | CON 21 | INT 19 | WIS 12 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe wastrilith can breathe air and water.\n\nCorrupt Water\n\nAt the start of each of the wastrilith's turns, exposed water within 30 feet of it is befouled. Underwater, this effect lightly obscures the area until a current clears it away. Water in containers remains corrupted until it evaporates.\n\nA creature that consumes this foul water or swims in it must make a 18 Constitution saving throw. On a successful save, the creature is immune to the foul water for 24 hours. On a failed save, the creature takes 14 (4d6) poison damage and is poisoned for 1 minute. At the end of this time, the poisoned creature must repeat the saving throw. On a failure, the creature takes 18 (4d8) poison damage and is poisoned until it finishes a long rest.\n\nIf another demon drinks the foul water as an action, it gains 11 (2d10) temporary hit points.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe wastrilith has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe wastrilith makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks, and it uses Grasping Spout.\n\nBite\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h30 (4d12 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h18 (4d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nGrasping Spout\n\nThe wastrilith magically launches a spout of water at one creature it can see within 60 feet of it. The target must make a 17 Strength saving throw, and it has disadvantage if it's underwater. On a failed save, it takes 22 (4d8 + 4) acid damage and is pulled up to 60 feet toward the wastrilith. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage and isn't pulled.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nUndertow\n\nIf the wastrilith is underwater, it causes all water within 60 feet of it to be difficult terrain for other creatures until the start of its next turn."},
  ["creature.wastrilith.mtf2014"]={title="Wastrilith",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 139\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 157 (15d10 + 75)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 80\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 18 | CON 21 | INT 19 | WIS 12 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe wastrilith can breathe air and water.\n\nCorrupt Water\n\nAt the start of each of the wastrilith's turns, exposed water within 30 feet of it is befouled. Underwater, this effect lightly obscures the area until a current clears it away. Water in containers remains corrupted until it evaporates.\n\nA creature that consumes this foul water or swims in it must make a 18 Constitution saving throw. On a successful save, the creature is immune to the foul water for 24 hours. On a failed save, the creature takes 14 (4d6) poison damage and is poisoned for 1 minute. At the end of this time, the poisoned creature must repeat the saving throw. On a failure, the creature takes 18 (4d8) poison damage and is poisoned until it finishes a long rest.\n\nIf another demon drinks the foul water as an action, it gains 11 (2d10) temporary hit points.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe wastrilith has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nUndertow\n\nAs a bonus action when the wastrilith is underwater, it can cause all water within 60 feet of it to be difficult terrain for other creatures until the start of its next turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe wastrilith uses Grasping Spout and makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h30 (4d12 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h18 (4d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nGrasping Spout\n\nThe wastrilith magically launches a spout of water at one creature it can see within 60 feet of it. The target must make a 17 Strength saving throw, and it has disadvantage if it's underwater. On a failed save, it takes 22 (4d8 + 4) acid damage and is pulled up to 60 feet toward the wastrilith. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage and isn't pulled."},
  ["feature.watcher-s-will.tce2014.paladin.watchers.3"]={title="Watcher's Will",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 54\n\nYou can use your Channel Divinity to invest your presence with the warding power of your faith. As an action, you can choose a number of creatures you can see within 30 feet of you, up to a number equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one creature). For 1 minute, you and the chosen creatures have advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma saving throws."},
  ["feat.watchers.rhw2014"]={title="Watchers",subtitle="Feat - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 35\n\nSomething unnatural is always watching you, taking the form of scurrying vermin and other eerie creatures. You gain the following features.\n\nBorrowed Eyes\n\nYou always have the XPHB and XPHB spells prepared. You can cast each spell without a spell slot, and you must finish a XPHB before you can cast it in this way again. You can also cast these spells using spell slots you have of the appropriate level.\n\nHeightened Suspicion\n\nWhenever you take the XPHB action, you can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to any ability check made as part of that action.\n\nIncessant Watchers\n\nYou have XPHB on saving throws made against the XPHB spell.\n\nIn addition, immediately after you make a XPHB and roll a 1 on the d20, paranoia threatens to overwhelm you. Make a Wisdom saving throw (DC 13 plus your XPHB). On a failed save, you have XPHB on XPHB for 1 minute. You can repeat the save at the end of each of your turns, ending the effect early on a success."},
  ["charoption.watchers.vrgr2014"]={title="Watchers",subtitle="Opcao de Personagem - VRGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\nSomething is always watching you and draws ethereal spirits that take the form of creatures made of shadowstuff, usually in the shape of Tiny beasts, that follow you and gather in your general vicinity. These creatures act like normal examples of their kind, but their behavior suggests a hint of malice. No matter what precautions you take, you can't permanently drive these spirits away. They always return, wait just beyond the reach of deterrents, or later crawl out of your clothes and equipment.\n\nRoll on or choose an option from the Watchers table to determine what sorts of forms the spirits typically take when they follow you.\n\nd8 | Watchers\n\n1 | Carrion Eaters. Jackals, ravens, vultures\n\n2 | Inescapable Judgments. Animate tools of punishment, drifting eyeballs, religious iconography\n\n3 | Night Wings. Bats, moths, owls\n\n4 | Plague Carriers. Fleas, rats, squirrels\n\n5 | Unnatural Observers. Animate objects, clockwork devices, otherworldly voyeurs\n\n6 | Sea Skulkers. Crabs, eels, jellyfish\n\n7 | Stray Souls. Ghost orbs, shadows, ectoplasmic wisps\n\n8 | Venomous Vermin. Scorpions, serpents, spiders\n\nBorrowed Eyes\n\nAs an action, you can influence the presence guiding the watchers for 1 hour. For the duration, you gain advantage on Intelligence (Investigation) and Wisdom (Perception) checks, and you can't be blinded. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest.\n\nDread Presence\n\nYou have disadvantage on Charisma (Deception), Charisma (Performance), and Charisma (Persuasion) checks made against creatures that can see the watchers, and you have disadvantage on saving throws made against the scrying spell.\n\nYou can temporarily disperse or hide the watchers with some effort. With 1 minute of work and a successful 15 Charisma (Animal Handling) check, you can suppress your Borrowed Eyes and Dread Presence for 1 hour. Once you successfully suppress these features, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest."},
  ["magicitem.watchful-helm.cm2014"]={title="Watchful Helm",subtitle="Item Magico - CM - 2014",body="Pagina: 183\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile you wear this helm, you gain a +1 bonus to AC and remain aware of your surroundings even while you're asleep, and you have advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\nAs a bonus action, you can cast the see invisibility spell from the helm. Once this property of the helm is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["spell.water-breathing.phb2014"]={title="Water Breathing",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 287\n\nThis spell grants up to ten willing creatures you can see within range the ability to breathe underwater until the spell ends. Affected creatures also retain their normal mode of respiration."},
  ["spell.water-breathing.xphb2024"]={title="Water Breathing",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 340\n\nThis spell grants up to ten willing creatures of your choice within range the ability to breathe underwater until the spell ends. Affected creatures also retain their normal mode of respiration."},
  ["creature.water-elemental.mm2014"]={title="Water Elemental",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 125\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 114 (12d10 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 90\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 18 | INT 5 | WIS 10 | CHA 8\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Aquan\n\nResistencias: acid\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nWater Form\n\nThe elemental can enter a hostile creature's space and stop there. It can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing.\n\nFreeze\n\nIf the elemental takes cold damage, it partially freezes; its speed is reduced by 20 feet until the end of its next turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe elemental makes two slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage.\n\nWhelm {@recharge 4}\n\nEach creature in the elemental's space must make a 15 Strength saving throw. On a failure, a target takes 13 (2d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage. If it is Large or smaller, it is also grappled (escape 14). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained and unable to breathe unless it can breathe water. If the saving throw is successful, the target is pushed out of the elemental's space.\n\nThe elemental can grapple one Large creature or up to two Medium or smaller creatures at one time. At the start of each of the elemental's turns, each target grappled by it takes 13 (2d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage. A creature within 5 feet of the elemental can pull a creature or object out of it by taking an action to make a 14 Strength check and succeeding."},
  ["creature.water-elemental.xmm2024"]={title="Water Elemental",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 322\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 114 (12d10 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 90\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 18 | INT 5 | WIS 10 | CHA 8\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Primordial (Aquan)\n\nResistencias: acid, fire\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFreeze\n\nIf the elemental takes Cold damage, its XPHB decreases by 20 feet until the end of its next turn.\n\nWater Form\n\nThe elemental can enter an enemy's space and stop there. It can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch without expending extra movement to do so.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe elemental makes two Slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nm 7, reach 5 ft. h13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition.\n\nWhelm {@recharge 4}\n\nstr 15, each creature in the elemental's space. actSaveFail 22 (4d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 14). Until the grapple ends, the target has the XPHB condition, is suffocating unless it can breathe water, and takes 9 (2d8) Bludgeoning damage at the start of each of the elemental's turns. The elemental can grapple one Large creature or up to two Medium or smaller creatures at a time with Whelm. As an action, a creature within 5 feet of the elemental can pull a creature out of it by succeeding on a 14 Strength (XPHB) check. actSaveSuccess Half damage only."},
  ["creature.water-elemental-myrmidon.mpmm2014"]={title="Water Elemental Myrmidon",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 123\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 127 (17d8 + 51)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, swim: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 8 | WIS 10 | CHA 10\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Aquan, one language of its creator's choice\n\nResistencias: acid\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe myrmidon makes three Trident attacks.\n\nTrident\n\nmw,rw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) force damage, or 8 (1d8 + 4) force damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack.\n\nFreezing Strikes {@recharge}\n\nThe myrmidon uses Multiattack. Each attack that hits deals an extra 5 (1d10) cold damage. A target that is hit by one or more of these attacks has its speed reduced by 10 feet until the end of the myrmidon's next turn."},
  ["creature.water-elemental-myrmidon.mtf2014"]={title="Water Elemental Myrmidon",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 203\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 127 (17d8 + 51)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, swim: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 8 | WIS 10 | CHA 10\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Aquan, one language of its creator's choice\n\nResistencias: acid\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe myrmidon's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe myrmidon makes three trident attacks.\n\nTrident\n\nmw,rw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage, or 8 (1d8 + 4) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack.\n\nFreezing Strikes {@recharge}\n\nThe myrmidon uses Multiattack. Each attack that hits deals an extra 5 (1d10) cold damage. A target that is hit by one or more of these attacks has its speed reduced by 10 feet until the end of the myrmidon's next turn."},
  ["creature.water-totem-elemental.psx2014"]={title="Water Totem Elemental",subtitle="Criatura - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["spell.water-walk.phb2014"]={title="Water Walk",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 287\n\nThis spell grants the ability to move across any liquid surface—such as water, acid, mud, snow, quicksand, or lava—as if it were harmless solid ground (creatures crossing molten lava can still take damage from the heat). Up to ten willing creatures you can see within range gain this ability for the duration.\n\nIf you target a creature submerged in a liquid, the spell carries the target to the surface of the liquid at a rate of 60 feet per round."},
  ["spell.water-walk.xphb2024"]={title="Water Walk",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 340\n\nThis spell grants the ability to move across any liquid surface—such as water, acid, mud, snow, quicksand, or lava—as if it were harmless solid ground (creatures crossing molten lava can still take damage from the heat). Up to ten willing creatures of your choice within range gain this ability for the duration.\n\nAn affected target must take a XPHB to pass from the liquid's surface into the liquid itself and vice versa, but if the target falls into the liquid, the target passes through the surface into the liquid below."},
  ["creature.water-weird.mm2014"]={title="Water Weird",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 299\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 58 (9d10 + 9)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, swim: 60\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 16 | CON 13 | INT 11 | WIS 10 | CHA 10\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Aquan but doesn't speak\n\nResistencias: fire\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, grappled, paralyzed, poisoned, restrained, prone, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nInvisible in Water\n\nThe water weird is invisible while fully immersed in water.\n\nWater Bound\n\nThe water weird dies if it leaves the water to which it is bound or if that water is destroyed.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nConstrict\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 10 ft., one creature. h13 (3d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage. If the target is Medium or smaller, it is grappled (escape 13) and pulled 5 feet toward the water weird. Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, the water weird tries to drown it, and the water weird can't constrict another target."},
  ["creature.water-weird.xmm2024"]={title="Water Weird",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 323\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 65 (10d10 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, swim: 60\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 16 | CON 13 | INT 11 | WIS 10 | CHA 10\n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Primordial but can't speak\n\nResistencias: fire\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nInvisible in Water\n\nThe water weird has the XPHB condition while fully immersed in water.\n\nWater Bound\n\nThe water weird dies if it leaves the water to which it is bound or if that water is destroyed.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSurge\n\nm 5, reach 10 ft. h13 (3d6 + 3) Cold damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 13), and it has the XPHB condition until the grapple ends."},
}
